                  "note": "Fake peer sends a non-JSON text frame before the Browser.getVersion reply. Listener exc is JSONDecodeError, nothing is logged, and send stays pending after 3s with mapper=[1]. Stuck at connection.py:662 send `return await tx`. A malformed Target.detachedFromTarget with no params.sessionId gives KeyError('sessionId') from _receive_message with the same hang. A second reader on the websocket (artificial setup) kills the listener with ConcurrencyError. Refinement: the tx stays in mapper, so the hang ends at the next send() on that connection (that run printed 'original done=True result=P'). I found no natural trigger in zendriver for the ConcurrencyError or the non-JSON frame, so the triggers are defensive / low realism even though the mechanism is real."
