                  "note": "Fake peer sends Target.targetCreated and then the Browser.getVersion reply. Handlers registered: `async def bad(): pass` then a good one. Repo: send hangs, listener exc TypeError('...bad_handler() takes 0 positional arguments but 1 was given') raised at listener_loop line ~1000 after the warning log. Prototype (inner `raise` removed): send returns, listener running, good handler called once."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "A2.4",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Browser-free: browser Connection plus a flat-session tab Connection (owner namespace). After the browser listener stops, the repo's tab.send hangs at connection.py:662. Real Chromium: a browser-level custom Target.getTargets whose parser raises -> 'browser listener running: False exc: notThere', then 'tab.evaluate after browser-level failure: HUNG (> 5s)'; prototype returns 4. Correction to the finder's repro: Runtime.evaluate on browser.connection gets a CDP error reply (no Runtime domain on the browser target), so it raises and does not kill the listener. A browser-domain command is needed. Once the other hunks are in, this path is reachable only through the receive-error break, but hunk 3 depends on it so that tabs recover."
