              ],
              "evidence": "Scratch dir /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/Q1-fixsafety/. The regression test test_q1_listener_robustness.py has 9 cases; all are browser-free and use a scripted fake websocket that monkeypatches websockets.connect, like tests/core/test_connection.py. Each call is bounded with asyncio.wait(timeout=3), and the stuck task's stack is printed. Repo py3.13 (no PYTHONPATH): 'zendriver imported from: /home/user/zendriver/zendriver/__init__.py' / '9 failed in 27.36s'; every stuck stack is at 'File \"/home/user/zendriver/zendriver/core/connection.py\", line 662, in send: return await tx'. Prototype py3.13 (PYTHONPATH=<dir>/pkg): 'zendriver imported from: .../Q1-fixsafety/pkg/zendriver/__init__.py' / '9 passed in 0.25s'. Python 3.11.17 venv: repo '9 failed in 27.59s', prototype '9 passed in 0.40s'. Ablation (prototype minus one hunk each): without the Transaction.__call__ hunk 4 tests fail (parse cases); without the aopen-revive hunk 2 fail (tab tests); without the receive-except hunk 3 fail; without the removed `raise` 1 fails (bad handler). So every hunk is necessary, and each maps to one member. probe_listener_death.py on repo: missing-key -> exc=KeyError('targetInfo') mapper={}; custom-gen -> KeyError('notThere') mapper={}; non-json -> JSONDecodeError, tx still in mapper; bad-handler -> TypeError, tx in mapper. Real headless Chromium 141, probe_real_chrome.py, repo: tab.send(bad custom cmd) HUNG; browser.connection.send(bad Target.getTargets) HUNG with the browser listener dead; then tab.evaluate HUNG. Prototype: ProtocolException, ProtocolException, ok -> 4. Repo suite on the prototype with real Chromium (test_connection, test_tab, test_frames, test_browser, test_multiple_browsers, -m 'not external'): '68 passed, 4 deselected'; the import was checked as pkg/zendriver/core/connection.py. mypy: 'Found 332 errors in 47 files' on both the untouched copy and the prototype. All errors are in zendriver/cdp/ (path-exclude mismatch from the scratch path), none in core/connection.py, and the logs are identical after path normalisation. The repo was not modified (git status empty). All browsers I started were stopped.",
              "refinements": "(a) The finder's real-Chrome repro for A2.4 (Runtime.evaluate custom cmd on browser.connection) does not hang, because Chrome answers with an error since the browser target has no Runtime domain. Use a browser-domain method (Target.getTargets) instead. (b) Severity is per path. For parse failures the tx is popped and lost, so the hang is permanent and aclose cannot release it. For the bad-handler and receive-error paths the tx stays in mapper, so a later send() (which restarts the listener) or aclose() releases it. For tabs it is permanent unless something sends on browser.connection. (c) The receive-error fix must break, not continue: a continue-based handler freezes the whole event loop on py>=3.12 when the error is persistent and synchronous (shown with ConcurrencyError). (d) Optional, not in the prototype: set self.idle on listener exit, so a wait() already blocked on the dead listener's idle event returns. This is pre-existing for ConnectionClosed too. Once hunk 1 is in, parse failures no longer kill the listener, which covers A2.3's tab.wait() side claim for that path. (e) The outer `except Exception: raise` in dispatch becomes dead code and can be dropped in the real PR.",
              "chrome_claims": [
                {
                  "claim": "Against real headless Chromium 141, a tab (flat session) custom command whose result parser raises hangs tab.send on repo code and raises ProtocolException on the prototype; tab.evaluate keeps working afterwards",
