            "lens": "reproduce",
            "entry": {
              "group_id": "Q2",
              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "Confirmed on real headless Chromium (Python 3.13.16, scratch copy of the package). Tab.select/find/find_all/select_all/xpath/wait_for/__call__, cloudflare.cf_is_interactive_challenge_present and Tab.verify_cf all check their timeout only between CDP round trips. If the renderer never answers (an open alert(), or while(true){}), each call with timeout=2 was still pending after 8 s, and select and xpath were still pending after 30 s. Each one sits on an unbounded Transaction: DOM.getDocument, or DOM.enable for xpath. Under the same conditions the controls (wait_for_ready_state(timeout=2), already fixed in #291, and tab.wait(2)) returned after 2.00 s. If the renderer is busy for a finite 12 s, the same methods return 9 s late (11.2 to 11.7 s for timeout=2). Two smaller defects also reproduced. xpath(timeout<=0) never runs the query and returns [] even when the element exists, and with a positive timeout it spins with no sleep. verify_cf(timeout=1, click_delay=4) takes 4.02 s.",
              "member_verdicts": [
                {
                  "fid": "B13.1",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Real Chromium, alert and busy modes: select('#nope',timeout=2) was stuck at Tab.select (tab.py:351, query_selector) and select(include_frames=True) at tab.py:347 (_query_selector_all_with_frames); find(timeout=2) at Tab.find tab.py:308; find_all at Tab.find_all tab.py:382; select_all at Tab.select_all tab.py:423. Each one was waiting on Transaction DOM.getDocument (status pending) and was STILL PENDING after 8.00s; select was still pending after 30.00s. Its sub-claim that self.sleep/update_target is one more unbounded send was not observed in any stack (Target.getTargetInfo is answered by the browser, not the renderer)."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "A5.1",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Same runs as B13.1. Also xpath('//nope', timeout=2), documented as 'will not raise' and to return [], was stuck at Tab.xpath tab.py:473 on Transaction DOM.enable (pending) in alert, busy and busy12 modes, and still pending after 30.00s with alert. Busy 12s: select(timeout=2) raised its TimeoutError only after 11.20s, and xpath returned [] after 11.20s."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "B13.2",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "wait_for(selector='#nope',timeout=2) was stuck at Tab.wait_for tab.py:1308 and wait_for(text=...) at tab.py:1316, both on DOM.getDocument. tab(selector='#nope',timeout=2) was stuck at Tab.__call__ tab.py:1966. xpath was stuck at tab.py:473 on DOM.enable. All were still pending after 8s (alert and busy). Side observation: __call__ passes (text, selector, timeout) positionally into wait_for(selector, text, timeout), so the arguments are swapped. This is a separate bug that does not change the hang."
