                }
              ],
              "evidence": "Commands, run from /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/Q2-reproduce with PYTHONPATH=<that dir>/pkg (a scratch copy; the probes print zendriver.__file__ from pkg/ and python 3.13.16), PATH including the scratchpad chromium symlink, and PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1:\n(1) `timeout 300 /home/user/zendriver/.venv/bin/python probe_real.py alert` and `... busy`. Each case opens a new tab with a data: page, runs setTimeout(()=>alert('blocking'),200) or setTimeout(()=>{while(true){}},200), sleeps 1s, starts the call as a task, waits up to 8s with asyncio.wait, then prints task.print_stack(). Key lines: `[alert] select: STILL PENDING after 8.00s (timeout=2); ... Tab.select() running at .../tab.py:351> wait_for=<Transaction method: DOM.getDocument status: pending>`; `[alert] xpath: STILL PENDING ... tab.py:473 ... method: DOM.enable`; `[alert] wait_for_sel: ... tab.py:1308`; `[alert] call_sel: ... tab.py:1966`; `[alert] cf_present: ... cloudflare.py:120 ... DOM.getDocument`; `[alert] verify_cf: ... tab.py:1666 ... DOM.getDocument`; controls `[alert] CTRL_wait_for_ready_state: DONE in 2.00s -> raised TimeoutError` and `[alert] CTRL_wait: DONE in 2.01s`. The busy run gave the same results for all 11 cases.\n(2) `OUTER=30 timeout 120 ... probe_real.py alert select xpath` -> `[alert] select: STILL PENDING after 30.00s (timeout=2)` and `[alert] xpath: STILL PENDING after 30.00s (timeout=2)`.\n(3) `OUTER=25 timeout 250 ... probe_real.py busy12 select wait_for_sel xpath cf_present verify_cf CTRL_wait_for_ready_state` (12s busy loop) -> select TimeoutError in 11.20s, xpath [] in 11.20s, wait_for_sel TimeoutError in 11.20s, cf_present False in 11.70s, verify_cf TimeoutError in 11.70s; control 2.00s.\n(4) `timeout 150 ... probe_xpath_cf.py` -> xpath timeout=0 / -1 returns [] while the element exists; the miss made 1290 sends in 0.5s; `verify_cf(timeout=1, click_delay=4) raised TimeoutError: Could not solve the checkbox in 1 seconds (timeout during clicks). after 4.02s clicks=1`.\nAll chromium pids I started (19468, 19632, 19634, 19636, 24124, 24678 and the probe_xpath_cf instance) were stopped with browser.stop(), and no chrome processes remain. The newest /tmp/uc_* profile dirs date from before my runs, so mine were removed.",
              "refinements": "The root cause matches the claim: each polling loop compares loop.time() with its deadline only after an awaited CDP round trip returns, and none of those awaits (DOM.getDocument in query_selector / query_selector_all / find_elements_by_text / cf_find_interactive_challenge, and DOM.enable in xpath) is bounded. In alert mode the hang is effectively forever: the Transaction stays pending as long as the dialog is open (seen for 30s). In finite-busy mode the deadline is overrun by the busy duration. Other observations: (a) the self.sleep -> update_target send (Target.getTargetInfo) never showed up as a blocking point, because the browser answers it even when the renderer is blocked; (b) Tab.__call__ passes its arguments to wait_for positionally in swapped order (text into selector), which is a separate bug that does not change the hang; (c) A11.4 and A5.7 are timing/contract bugs (wrong-result) rather than hangs, but they share the same files and would naturally be fixed together. A fix that wraps each polling body in asyncio.wait_for(remaining) must keep each method's documented outcome on timeout: TimeoutError for find, select, find_all, select_all, wait_for and verify_cf; [] for xpath; False for cf_is_interactive_challenge_present. The fix should also cancel the stuck Transaction cleanly.",
              "chrome_claims": [
                {
