          {
            "lens": "fixsafety",
            "entry": {
              "group_id": "Q2",
              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "Confirmed on real headless Chromium and with browser-free tests. When the renderer stops answering (an open alert()), find, select, find_all, select_all, wait_for, tab(), xpath, cf_is_interactive_challenge_present and verify_cf all hang forever. Each loop checks its timeout only after an unbounded CDP await returns. On a page with a busy main thread they overrun the timeout by the length of the busy period. verify_cf also overruns by up to click_delay. xpath(timeout<=0) never makes an attempt, and with a positive timeout it busy-loops. The triage fix (wrap each loop in asyncio.wait_for(..., timeout), as #291 did) cures the hang but is NOT safe as written: it causes three confirmed regressions. A safer minimal-local variant was prototyped. It also needs a one-line companion fix in Connection._register_handlers, whose bare `except:` swallows the timeout's CancelledError and leaves the call hanging and uncancellable.",
              "member_verdicts": [
                {
                  "fid": "B13.1",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Real Chromium, alert open: select/find/find_all/select_all('#nope'/'nope', timeout=1) were still pending after 8 s. Stacks showed Tab.select tab.py:351, Tab.find :308, Tab.find_all :382 and Tab.select_all :423, each awaiting a pending DOM.getDocument Transaction. Busy-loop mode (6 s while loop): each raised only after 5.75 s. Control: wait_for_ready_state(timeout=1) raised after 1.00 s. Browser-free tests (query_selector, find_element_by_text, find_elements_by_text or query_selector_all patched to hang; also get_frames hanging with include_frames=True) fail on the repo and pass on the prototype."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "A5.1",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Same reproduction as B13.1. In addition, xpath('//nope', timeout=1) was stuck at Tab.xpath tab.py:473 on a pending DOM.enable (an unbounded send(cdp.dom.enable(), True) in every pass)."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "B13.2",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Real Chromium, alert open: wait_for(selector='#nope', timeout=1) was stuck at Tab.wait_for tab.py:1308 (DOM.getDocument), tab(selector=...) at Tab.__call__ :1966, and xpath at :473 (DOM.enable), all still pending after 8 s. Side finding, a separate bug: Tab.__call__ passes (text, selector) positionally into wait_for(selector, text), so tab(selector=x) actually runs a text search."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "A6.5",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Alert: wait_for never returns (pending after 8 s on DOM.getDocument at tab.py:1308). Busy 6 s renderer: wait_for(selector, timeout=1) raised only after 5.75 s. Also found while fixing: wait_for sleeps 0.5 s even after a hit, so a strict wait_for bound throws away an element it has already found (see risks)."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "B13.3",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Real Chromium, alert open: cf_is_interactive_challenge_present(tab, timeout=1) was pending after 8 s at cloudflare.py:120 (cf_wait_for_interactive_challenge to DOM.getDocument). tab.verify_cf(timeout=1) was pending at tab.py:1666 on DOM.getDocument. Busy: they took 6.25 s instead of 1 s. Click phase, browser-free (query_selector hangs after the first lookup): the repo hits the 6 s outer safety net, the prototype raises TimeoutError after 1.5 s."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "A11.4",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Browser-free fake (challenge found, input never gets a value): verify_cf(timeout=1, click_delay=4) raised TimeoutError after 4.01 s on the repo and 1.00 s on the prototype. The deadline is checked only at the top of the click loop, and asyncio.sleep(click_delay) in cloudflare.verify_cf is unbounded. The cf_wait_for_interactive_challenge scan overrun was seen on a busy page (6.25 s for timeout=1)."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "A5.7",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Real Chromium: xpath('//p[@id=\"topp\"]', timeout=0) returned [] while the default timeout returned 1 element (the loop condition is false before the first pass). One miss with xpath('//nope', timeout=0.5) issued 1272 CDP sends (busy loop with no sleep). The prototype returns the element for timeout=0 and makes 13 sends in 0.5 s. Browser-free: 1,444,228 attempts in 1 s with no-op sends."
                }
              ],
              "evidence": "Probes (my own, outer `timeout` plus asyncio.wait for 8 s, Python 3.13.16, websockets 14.1, headless Chromium 141): /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/Q2-fixsafety/probe_chrome.py (modes alert|busy), probe_semantics.py and probe_swallow.py in the same dir. Repo, alert mode: all 9 methods STILL PENDING after 8.0 s with stacks on pending DOM.getDocument/DOM.enable Transactions; wait_for_ready_state control 1.00 s. Repo, busy mode: 5.75-6.25 s for timeout=1. Final prototype (pkg3): alert and busy modes all raise or return the documented outcome (TimeoutError with the original message, [] for xpath, False for cf_is_interactive_challenge_present) after 1.50 s. After dismissing the dialog (Page.enable is needed before the dialog opens for Page.handleJavaScriptDialog to see it), select, find and xpath work again on both repo and prototype; the mapper drains to 0 and no loop or logging errors appear.\n\nRegression tests: tests_q2/test_q2_timeouts.py (24 tests) and tests_q2/test_q2_fake_peer.py (2 tests, a websocket fake CDP peer that never answers DOM.*).\n- Repo (zendriver from /home/user/zendriver/zendriver/__init__.py): test_q2_timeouts gives '15 failed, 9 passed in 82.30s'. The 9 passing tests are behaviour-preservation tests. In test_q2_fake_peer, test_select_times_out_over_websocket FAILED ('1 failed in 6.25s', only the safety net fired) and test_select_times_out_with_pending_domain_enable was killed by `timeout 30` (exit 124).\n- Prototype pkg3 (zendriver from .../Q2-fixsafety/pkg3/zendriver/__init__.py): '26 passed in 27.58s'.\n- Same results on Python 3.10.20 and 3.11.17 scratch venvs (untouched copy: 15 failed, 9 passed; prototype: 24 passed). This matters for verify_cf, because on 3.10 asyncio.TimeoutError is not the builtin TimeoutError.\n- Repo suite tests/core (copied to scratch, real Chromium, -n 3): untouched copy '109 passed, 1 skipped'; pkg2 and pkg3 '109 passed, 1 skipped'.\n- mypy (uv run mypy --config-file pyproject.toml <copy>/zendriver): output identical between the untouched copy and pkg, pkg2 and pkg3 (all 332 errors are in cdp/, 0 in core/). ruff check and ruff format are clean.\n- The strict-wrap variant (pkg, the triage hypothesis) fails 4 of the behaviour-preservation tests. On real Chromium: an element appearing at 0.3 s with select('#late', timeout=0.5) was found by the repo after 0.504 s, while the strict wrap raised TimeoutError after 0.500 s; appearing at 0.7 s with timeout=1, the repo found it after 1.008 s and the strict wrap raised after 1.001 s. pkg2/pkg3 found both (0.504 s and 1.003 s). asyncio.wait_for(coro, 0) never runs the coroutine (checked on 3.13 and 3.10).",
              "refinements": "Locations (repo HEAD 064148f): unbounded awaits in Tab.find tab.py:308, Tab.select :351, Tab.find_all :382, Tab.select_all :423, Tab.xpath :473 (DOM.enable) and :474, Tab.wait_for :1308, Tab.__call__ :1966, cloudflare.cf_wait_for_interactive_challenge (scan loop), cf_is_interactive_challenge_present :120, and the verify_cf click loop (check_input, mouse_click, asyncio.sleep(click_delay)).\n\nOne cause sits outside the listed files: Connection._register_handlers (connection.py:709) uses a bare `except:` around `await self.send(domain_mod.enable(), _is_update=True)`. It swallows the CancelledError delivered by any timeout, so the outer send() goes on to re-send the enable and await it again. Whenever a handler exists for a domain whose enable the renderer does not answer (e.g. tab.add_handler(cdp.dom.DocumentUpdated, ...) added while a dialog is open), every bounded call hangs and cannot be cancelled. Even an outer asyncio.wait_for cannot stop it: confirmed on real Chromium and with the fake peer. This also defeats the existing #291 wait_for_ready_state fix. Narrowing it to `except Exception:` fixes it. A more careful variant would also remove domain_mod from enabled_domains on CancelledError and re-raise, so a cancelled enable gets re-sent later.\n\nSeparate bug, not in this group: Tab.__call__ passes (text, selector) positionally to wait_for(selector, text), so the two arguments are swapped. element.py:576 has another bare except that swallows CancelledError (around Element.flash in Element.mouse_click), outside the Q2 paths.",
              "chrome_claims": [
                {
                  "claim": "Chromium does not answer DOM.getDocument or DOM.enable on a page session while an alert() dialog is open",
                  "status": "verified",
                  "how": "probe_chrome.py alert mode on headless Chromium 141: task stacks show <Transaction method: DOM.getDocument / DOM.enable status: pending> 8 s after the call"
                },
                {
                  "claim": "A busy renderer main thread delays DOM.* replies until the busy period ends",
                  "status": "verified",
                  "how": "probe_chrome.py busy mode (6 s while loop started via setTimeout): timeout=1 calls returned after 5.75-6.25 s on the repo"
                },
                {
                  "claim": "After the dialog is dismissed Chromium answers the queued commands. The Listener pops the cancelled Transactions without error and the tab works again",
                  "status": "verified",
                  "how": "probe_semantics.py: after Page.handleJavaScriptDialog, select/find/xpath succeed in a few ms, len(tab.mapper)==0, no loop exception handler or ERROR log records"
                },
                {
                  "claim": "Page.handleJavaScriptDialog reports 'No dialog is showing' unless the Page domain was enabled before the dialog opened",
                  "status": "verified",
                  "how": "probe_semantics.py first run without Page.enable got ProtocolException 'No dialog is showing'; with cdp.page.enable() sent first, the dismiss worked"
                }
              ],
              "realism": "high",
              "severity": "hang",
              "fix_assessment": {
                "kind": "minimal-local",
                "prototype_dir": "/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/Q2-fixsafety/pkg3",
                "diff_summary": "Diffs are in tab_final.diff, cloudflare_final.diff and connection_v3.diff in /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/Q2-fixsafety/ (the strict-wrap variant for comparison is in .../pkg).\n(1) tab.py: new module helper _poll_with_timeout(poll, timeout, message). If timeout <= 0 it awaits poll unbounded, which keeps the single attempt. Otherwise it runs asyncio.wait_for(poll, timeout + 0.5) and turns asyncio.TimeoutError into asyncio.TimeoutError(message).\n(2) find, select, find_all and select_all keep their loops unchanged inside a nested _poll() and return await _poll_with_timeout(...). The 0.5 s sleep is clamped to min(0.5, deadline - now), so the last attempt happens at the deadline and the 0.5 s grace lets it finish.\n(3) wait_for: same wrap, and it sleeps only after a miss (a strict bound would cut the trailing sleep and throw away an element already found).\n(4) xpath: a while-True _poll that always makes at least one attempt, stops when items are found or elapsed >= timeout, sleeps with the same clamp instead of busy-looping, and returns [] on the bound.\n(5) cloudflare.py: cf_wait_for_interactive_challenge wraps its scan loop in asyncio.wait_for(_poll(), timeout + 0.5) and returns (None, None, None) on timeout. verify_cf moves the click phase verbatim into _cf_click_challenge(...), bounded by asyncio.wait_for(..., time left + 0.5). On the bound it raises builtin TimeoutError (needed for 3.10) with the existing 'timeout during clicks' message. asyncio.sleep(click_delay) is clamped to the deadline.\n(6) connection.py:709: `except:` becomes `except Exception:` in Connection._register_handlers, so a timeout's CancelledError is no longer swallowed.",
                "regression_test_path": "/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/Q2-fixsafety/tests_q2/test_q2_timeouts.py (also tests_q2/test_q2_fake_peer.py in the same dir)",
                "fails_on_repo": "yes",
                "passes_on_prototype": "yes",
                "mypy_ok": "yes",
                "risks": "(a) The triage hypothesis, a strict asyncio.wait_for(loop, timeout) as in #291, is unsafe as written:\n- wait_for(..., <=0) never runs the attempt. That breaks timeout=0 one-shot checks, and xpath's internal find_all(xpath, timeout=0) would then always return [].\n- It cuts the trailing 0.5 s sleep, so the last attempt is lost. Confirmed on Chromium: elements appearing 0.3 s into timeout=0.5, or 0.7 s into timeout=1, are found by the repo but get TimeoutError with the strict wrap.\n- wait_for's sleep after a hit gets cut, so an element it already found is discarded.\nThe prototype avoids all three with the timeout<=0 bypass, a grace of one poll interval, clamped sleeps and no sleep after a hit.\n(b) The companion fix in Connection._register_handlers is required. Without it, a pending domain enable (a handler registered while the page is blocked) makes the call hang and become uncancellable, and the same applies to the existing wait_for_ready_state fix.\n(c) Behaviour changes callers may notice:\n- A blocked page now raises or returns at timeout+0.5 s instead of hanging.\n- wait_for and tab() return as soon as the element is found (no 0.5 s trailing sleep) and give up at about timeout instead of timeout+0.5.\n- The last find/select attempt happens at the deadline instead of up to 0.5 s after it.\n- xpath polls every 0.5 s instead of spinning (13 vs 1272 sends in 0.5 s), so an element can be found up to 0.5 s later. timeout<=0 now makes one attempt and can return elements where it used to return [].\n- verify_cf's click_delay sleeps are clamped to the deadline, so solves that were only detected after the deadline now raise TimeoutError, as the docstring says they should.\n(d) timeout<=0 deliberately keeps one unbounded attempt, so it still hangs on a blocked renderer, as query_selector does.\n(e) Cancellation side effects (the same as with #291):\n- xpath cancelled between DOM.enable and disable leaves the DOM agent enabled.\n- A cancelled performSearch leaves a search session open in the browser.\n- A cancelled Transaction stays in mapper until Chrome replies (verified it drains once the dialog is dismissed).\n- A cancelled first-time _attach_session can leak a browser-side session.\n(f) No lock is held across the bounded region. _open_lock and _attach_lock are released by `async with` on cancel, and the helper takes no lock, so there is no re-entrancy or deadlock issue. Nested calls are fine: xpath calls find_all(timeout=0) from inside its bounded poll.\n(g) Builtin vs asyncio TimeoutError: on 3.10 they differ. verify_cf converts explicitly, and the tab methods keep asyncio.TimeoutError. Verified on 3.10.20, 3.11.17 and 3.13.16.\n(h) The 0.5 s grace is a heuristic. A final attempt that takes longer than 0.5 s on a very heavy page is cut, giving TimeoutError where the repo would have returned the result."
              }
            }
          }
        ]
      },
