        "lenses": [
          {
            "lens": "reproduce",
            "entry": {
              "group_id": "Q3",
              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "Reproduced every member with my own probes, on real headless Chromium 141 and on a browser-free fake CDP peer. (1) Browser._stop awaits Target.detachFromTarget (inside Connection.aclose, connection.py:517) and Browser.close (browser.py:883), and neither has a timeout. A frozen or unresponsive browser therefore makes stop() hang forever before it reaches terminate/kill. Bounding stop() with wait_for leaves the process alive and the profile on disk, and the atexit hook has already been unregistered, so nothing cleans up later. (2) If Chrome dies just before stop(), Connection.aclose raises ConnectionClosedError, because it only catches ProtocolException. The exception aborts _stop: _process stays set, the process is never reaped and the profile leaks. (3) Two concurrent stop() calls race in the terminate/poll loop and one raises AttributeError 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'poll' at _stop:901. (4) Under asyncio.run, the atexit cleanup always fails at `await asyncio.to_thread(self._process.wait)` (_stop:909) with RuntimeError('Executor shutdown has been called'), so the /tmp/uc_* profile leaks. This happens on Python 3.13 and 3.11, and also on the Ctrl+C path. Tab.close() also hangs well past the 10 s its docstring promises, stuck at Tab.close:1079 -> Connection.send.",
              "member_verdicts": [
                {
                  "fid": "B13.5",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "r_sigstop.py (real Chromium, tab attached, SIGSTOP). After 12 s stop() was still pending; await chain Browser.stop:872 -> Browser._stop:879 -> Connection.aclose:517 -> Connection.send:662, waiting on 'Transaction method: Target.detachFromTarget status: pending'; proc state T, _process still set. After cancelling: proc alive True, profile exists True, not in registry. r_sigstop_exit.py: wait_for(stop(),5) timed out; after asyncio.run (atexit hooks ran) proc alive True state T, profile exists True. Fake peer r_fake.py close_silent: no targets, peer never answers Browser.close; stop() pending at Browser._stop:883 -> Connection.send:662, fake process still running. Tab.close sub-claim: r_sigstop_exit.py tabclose: 'tab.close() done=False after 25.0s, stuck at: Tab.close:1079 -> Connection.send:662', so no TimeoutError at 10 s."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "A3.4",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Same root cause and same repro as B13.5. With SIGSTOP, stop() was still pending after 12 s, waiting on the Target.detachFromTarget Transaction; terminate/kill was never reached (proc state T). After wait_for times out, nothing kills Chrome at exit: atexit is unregistered and the instance is gone from the registry, so the process stays alive and the profile stays on disk after asyncio.run returns. I did not test the stderr-pipe variant (separate finding)."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "B15.3",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
