              "evidence": "All commands were run from /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/Q3-reproduce/ with PATH including the scratchpad chromium, using /home/user/zendriver/.venv/bin/python (3.13.16, websockets 14.1), each under `timeout 90-120`, plus an inner asyncio.wait_for or asyncio.wait with a positive timeout.\n- `python r_sigstop.py attached`: 'stop() STILL PENDING after 12s', chain 'Browser.stop browser.py:872 / Browser._stop browser.py:879 / Connection.aclose connection.py:517 / Connection.send connection.py:662', wait_for=<Transaction method: Target.detachFromTarget status: pending>, 'proc state: T', 'after cancelling stop: proc alive: True profile exists: True', 'in registry: False'.\n- `python r_sigstop_exit.py stop`: 'wait_for(stop(), 5) -> TimeoutError', then 'after asyncio.run (atexit hooks ran): proc alive: True state: T | profile exists: True'.\n- `python r_sigstop_exit.py tabclose`: 'tab.close() done=False after 25.0s', 'stuck at: Tab.close:1079 -> Connection.send:662'.\n- `python r_fake.py close_silent`: 'stop() STILL PENDING after 8s: Browser.stop:872 -> Browser._stop:883 -> Connection.send:662', 'proc returncode (None = still running): None | b._process still set: True | profile exists: True'.\n- `python r_fake.py detach_silent`: pending at Browser._stop:879 -> Connection.aclose:517 -> Connection.send:662, process still running.\n- `python r_fake.py detach_abort`: 'stop() RAISED ConnectionClosedError no close frame received or sent | tb: stop:872 -> _stop:879 -> aclose:517 -> send:662 -> listener_loop:925 ...', process still running, profile exists.\n- `python r_crash_stop.py 0` x5: ConnectionClosedError every run, '_process still set: True | profile exists: True'. `r_crash_stop.py 0.5`: stop ok, profile removed.\n- `STAGGER=0.4 python r_concurrent.py 12`: 7 of 12 runs gave \"AttributeError('NoneType' object has no attribute 'poll') @ stop:872->_stop:901\". `python r_fake.py concurrent` x3: AttributeError 3 of 3.\n- `python r_atexit.py plain|tb|ctx|sigint`: each printed 'Unhandled exception in asyncio atexit callback ... Executor shutdown has been called' and 'temp profile exists: True'. tb: _stop:909 asyncio.to_thread -> base_events.run_in_executor -> _check_default_executor -> RuntimeError.\n- Python 3.11.17 (throwaway venv, scratch copy of the package, zendriver.__file__ printed from pkg/): r_atexit.py plain and r_fake.py concurrent reproduced the same results.\nCleanup: every Chrome/sleep process I started was killed and reaped, my uc_* dirs were removed (the /tmp/uc_* count went back to 38, the pre-run baseline), the venv and package copy were deleted, and the repo's git status is clean.",
              "refinements": "- Root cause 1 (hang) has two independent unbounded awaits: the per-target Connection.aclose -> Target.detachFromTarget at connection.py:517, and Browser.close at browser.py:883. Either one alone hangs stop(), as the fake peer shows for each. A fix must bound both, or bound _stop's CDP phase as a whole, and must always fall through to terminate/kill. Tab.close has the same unbounded send at tab.py:1079 (Tab.close).\n- Root cause 2: Connection.aclose's session branch catches only ProtocolException. Because the listener fails pending transactions with the ConnectionClosed instance itself (listener_loop, _fail_pending_transactions(e)), ConnectionClosedError escapes. It aborts _stop before Browser.close, proxy-forwarder close, terminate/reap and profile removal. The same exception also breaks the atexit path when Chrome has died (seen in the tabclose run: 'Unhandled exception in asyncio atexit callback ...: no close frame received or sent', leaving a zombie and the profile).\n- A3.11: the race needs the two stop() calls to be offset (a stagger above a few ms). Simultaneous gather calls rarely hit it on real Chromium (0 of 8). The surviving call still removes the profile, so the impact is a spurious AttributeError, not a leak.\n- A3.1/B16.3: only the profile leaks. The process is terminated and reaped by the poll loop before the to_thread call fails. `async with await zd.start()` does not stop the browser in __aexit__, so the documented examples always rely on this broken atexit path.\n- stop() calls asyncio_atexit.unregister before _stop, so any hang or exception in _stop leaves nothing to clean up at exit.",
              "chrome_claims": [
                {
                  "claim": "A SIGSTOPped headless Chromium never answers Target.detachFromTarget, so stop() blocks before terminate/kill",
