                  "note": "Same mechanism and evidence as B13.5. p_waitfor_orphan.py: with `wait_for(b.stop(), 5)` on a SIGSTOPped Chrome followed by SIGCONT, Python exited and the Chrome pid stayed alive, reparented to ppid 1, with /tmp/uc_* still present. Nothing cleans up at exit, because stop() had already unregistered the asyncio_atexit hook and removed the instance from the registry."
                },
