                },
                {
                  "fid": "A1.2",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "p_kill.py: after browser._process.kill() with no delay, sleep(0), sleep(0.001) or sleep(0.003), `await stop()` raised ConnectionClosedError('no close frame received or sent') in 14/14 runs, with _process still set and the profile still present. With a sleep of 0.01 s or 0.1 s before stop(), 8/8 runs were clean. p_kill_blocking.py: Chrome SIGKILLed by an outside process while user code did 1 s of synchronous work, then stop() raised in 3/3 runs. Mitigations: a second stop() call succeeds and removes the profile, and an idle loop (await asyncio.sleep) is fine because the listener detaches the sessions first. The same escape is reached deterministically at the end of the hang path, after the keepalive timeout."
