              ],
              "evidence": "All probes are my own, in /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/Q3-refute/. Each prints zendriver.__file__=/home/user/zendriver/zendriver/__init__.py on Python 3.13.16, runs under `timeout`, and has an outer asyncio.wait/wait_for. p_atexit.py: atexit RuntimeError, profile exists True. p_sigstop.py attach/noattach: stop() pending at browser.py:872, wait_for=<Transaction Target.detachFromTarget pending>; process state T; after cancel the profile exists and b._process is set. p_sigstop_nosession.py: pending on the Browser.close Transaction. p_keepalive.py (PING_TIMEOUT=3): 'stop() finished after 33.0s exc=ConnectionClosedError(... keepalive ping timeout)', process state T, profile exists. p_waitfor_orphan.py: after Python exited, the Chrome pid was alive with ppid 1 and the profile existed. p_kill.py: the race window is about 3-10 ms. p_kill_blocking.py: 3/3 raised. p_kill_retry.py: a retry succeeds. p_concurrent.py: 1/10 AttributeError, 10/10 profiles removed. p_busy_renderer.py: a while(true){} renderer does not block stop() (0.40 s). p_stderr.py: Chrome's stderr stays at 5185 bytes after start, 20 navigations with console.error, and 5 new tabs. p_tabclose.py: Tab.close pending for over 13 s on Target.closeTarget. drive_ctrlc.py: Ctrl+C leaks the profile. Git history: the per-target aclose loop in _stop came in a51af21 (#278), when aclose only closed per-tab websockets, which close_timeout bounds. e81b66c (#280) made aclose a CDP round trip with only `except ProtocolException`. The to_thread wait came in 5c1a005. None of these commits shows the hang or the leak to be deliberate. No test asserts the current behaviour; test_browser_stop_exits_gracefully_without_kill (no kill, under 2 s on a healthy browser) is something a fix must keep passing. All browsers I started were killed and their /tmp/uc_* dirs removed. One running Chrome (parent probe_chrome.py) belongs to another verifier and was left alone.",
              "refinements": "Treat Q3 as four bugs that share one function. (a) Atexit leak: deterministic on Python 3.10+ (Runner.close calls shutdown_default_executor before loop.close) for any browser not stopped explicitly, including after Ctrl+C. Only the temp profile leaks plus the stderr message: Chrome is terminated and reaped. (b) Hang: only when the browser (main) process stops servicing DevTools: SIGSTOP or a frozen container/VM, a hung browser UI/IO thread, or a remote browser behind a silent network partition. A busy or infinite-looping renderer does NOT trigger it (verified). The stderr-pipe deadlock trigger is unlikely with the default flags, since only about 5 KB is written at startup (verified in this container). The keepalive bounds the wait at about 930 s, but stop() then raises ConnectionClosedError from aclose and still never terminates or kills Chrome. Cancelling stop() via wait_for orphans Chrome and the profile, because the atexit hook is already unregistered. (c) ConnectionClosedError escape: only if stop() starts before the listener has handled the socket close, i.e. within about 3-10 ms of browser death or after blocking synchronous work. A second stop() recovers. (d) Concurrent stop(): about 1 in 10 runs, only a spurious AttributeError in one caller, no leak. A fix must keep the healthy-path stop() fast and without kill (existing test asserts under 2 s and no kill).",
              "chrome_claims": [
                {
