          {
            "lens": "fixsafety",
            "entry": {
              "group_id": "Q3",
              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "I could not disprove any member; I reproduced all four failure modes in Browser._stop on the repo code. (1) An unresponsive browser makes stop() hang forever. The target.aclose() loop (Target.detachFromTarget, Connection.aclose:517) and the Browser.close send (_stop:883) have no timeout and run before terminate/kill. stop() has already unregistered the atexit hook (stop:870), so cancelling it with wait_for leaks the process and the profile. (2) If Chrome dies just before stop(), ConnectionClosedError escapes Connection.aclose (it only catches ProtocolException) and aborts _stop before terminate and profile cleanup. (3) Two stop() calls a little apart crash: one sets self._process=None while the other is in asyncio.sleep(0.25) and then calls self._process.poll() (_stop:901). (4) On the atexit path under asyncio.run, `await asyncio.to_thread(self._process.wait)` (_stop:909) raises RuntimeError('Executor shutdown has been called'), so the temp profile is left behind. A minimal fix in browser.py alone (about 30 lines) fixes all four. All 7 regression tests fail on the repo code and pass on the prototype under Python 3.13 and 3.11. The repo's own tests/core suite passes on the prototype, and mypy shows no new errors.",
              "member_verdicts": [
                {
                  "fid": "B13.5",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Real headless Chromium, Python 3.13: after tab.evaluate('1') and SIGSTOP, stop() was still pending after 10s. Its stack showed Browser.stop() at browser.py:872 waiting on 'Transaction method: Target.detachFromTarget status: pending'. After cancelling: process alive True, profile exists True. With a fake peer, stop() also hangs when only Browser.close goes unanswered. The Tab.close aside (close_target send outside wait_for(future, 10)) is confirmed by reading tab.py Tab.close only; I did not prototype it."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "A3.4",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Same root cause and reproduction as B13.5: SIGSTOP plus stop() is pending on Target.detachFromTarget and terminate()/kill() is never reached. Fake-peer test test_stop_terminates_an_unresponsive_browser[Target.detachFromTarget] fails on the repo code ('stop() still waiting ... after 10s') and passes on the prototype."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "B15.3",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Duplicate of A3.4/B13.5. Both unbounded steps (detach and Browser.close) hang independently: both parametrized fake-peer cases fail on the repo code."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "B16.2",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Hang confirmed as above. The claim that the atexit hook is dropped first is also confirmed: test_cancelled_stop_keeps_the_atexit_cleanup on the repo code shows asyncio_atexit callbacks == [] after wait_for(stop(), 0.5) times out, so nothing cleans up later. The prototype moves the unregister to after _stop()."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "A1.2",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Real Chromium, 3 of 3 runs: browser._process.kill() then stop() gives 'stop RAISED ConnectionClosedError no close frame received or sent | _process still set: True | profile exists: True'. Fake peer that aborts the TCP connection on Target.detachFromTarget: traceback stop:872 -> _stop:879 -> Connection.aclose:517 -> send:662 -> raised in listener_loop via _fail_pending_transactions(e). The prototype returns cleanly: process reaped, profile removed."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "A3.11",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "asyncio.gather(b.stop(), b.stop()) with no offset gave 0 of 9 failures on real Chromium. With the second stop() started 50-200 ms after the first it failed 12 of 12 times: ['AttributeError', 'NoneType']. The fake-process test with a 0.1 s offset fails deterministically. The calling task gets AttributeError, but the other stop() still removes the profile, so I saw no leak. The 'profile cleanup is skipped' part is true only for the call that crashed."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "A3.1",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Real Chromium with asyncio.run(main) and no stop(): stderr shows 'Unhandled exception in asyncio atexit callback <bound method Browser._atexit_cleanup ...>: Executor shutdown has been called' and the profile still exists afterwards. The fake-process test fails on the repo code in both the terminated and killed variants. The Ctrl+C path follows from Runner.close running in finally; I reasoned it but did not run it."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "B16.3",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Duplicate of A3.1, same reproduction. With the prototype the profile is removed and the process reaped on the atexit path, and nothing is printed to stderr."
                }
              ],
              "evidence": "Ran everything myself: Python 3.13.16, websockets 14.1, real headless Chromium plus a browser-free fake CDP peer. Regression test /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/Q3-fixsafety/tests/test_q3_stop_cleanup.py, 7 cases.\nREPO run (no PYTHONPATH): 'zendriver under test: /home/user/zendriver/zendriver/__init__.py' then FAILED x7: unresponsive[Target.detachFromTarget], unresponsive[Browser.close], connection_drops_during_detach, concurrent_stop, atexit[terminated], atexit[killed], cancelled_stop_keeps_the_atexit_cleanup -> '7 failed in 24.39s'.\nPROTOTYPE run (PYTHONPATH=.../Q3-fixsafety/pkg): 'zendriver under test: /tmp/.../Q3-fixsafety/pkg/zendriver/__init__.py' -> PASSED x7 -> '7 passed in 6.31s'.\nPython 3.11.17 throwaway venv gives the same result: untouched copy '7 failed in 24.63s', prototype '7 passed in 6.22s'.\nReal-Chromium probes (in .../Q3-fixsafety/probes/) on repo vs prototype:\n- SIGSTOP: repo 'stop done within 10s: False', stack on Target.detachFromTarget. Prototype 'stop done within WAIT: True elapsed 23.2 | process alive after: False profile exists: False'.\n- kill then stop: repo 'stop RAISED ConnectionClosedError' 3 of 3. Prototype 'stop OK _process still set: False profile exists: False' 3 of 3.\n- atexit: repo 'Unhandled exception ... Executor shutdown has been called' and 'profile exists: True'. Prototype 'profile exists: False'.\n- Concurrent stop with offset: repo 12 of 12 AttributeError. Prototype 12 of 12 [None, None].\nNo regressions: the repo's tests/core/test_browser.py (18 passed) and all of tests/core (-m 'not external', 104 passed, 1 skipped) pass on the prototype, using a copied tests dir so the prototype was imported. A healthy stop still takes 0.37 s on both. mypy --config-file pyproject.toml: 332 errors on both the prototype and an untouched copy, all in cdp/, so no new errors. ruff format and ruff check are clean.",
              "refinements": "1) Unresponsive-browser stop() is bounded on the prototype but takes about 23 s (5 s detach + 5 s Browser.close + about 10 s websockets close_timeout on a frozen peer + 3 s terminate wait, then kill). The 10 s close_timeout part is inferred from the 23.2 s total, not measured on its own. It could be cut by skipping Browser.close once the detach step timed out, or by passing a smaller close_timeout to websockets.connect. This is optional. 2) A3.11 never reproduced with zero offset (0 of 9 runs, and the earlier finder saw 2 of 7). It is deterministic once the second stop() starts 50-200 ms later, as with a signal-handler task plus a finally block. Only the late call raises; the profile is still removed by the other call. 3) The B13.5 aside about Tab.close (close_target send outside the 10 s wait_for) is real from reading the code, but it is a separate method; fix it separately if wanted. 4) Pre-existing and unrelated, also on the repo code: a normal stop() leaves the Popen stdin/stdout/stderr pipes unclosed (ResourceWarning under -W default). The atexit path also warns that 'Connection.send_context async generator was scheduled after loop.shutdown_asyncgens()'. 5) Connection.aclose still lets ConnectionClosed escape for other callers such as `async with tab:` (Connection.__aexit__). The _stop fix does not depend on changing that.",
