              "group_id": "Q4",
              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "Confirmed with real headless Chromium 141 on Python 3.13.16. Once util._start_process has spawned Chrome and Browser.start has added self to util.get_registered_instances(), any CancelledError (an asyncio.wait_for timeout, or Ctrl+C because asyncio.run cancels the main task) or any exception (update_targets, set_discover_targets, _read_headless_user_agent) leaves start() with no cleanup. Browser.create registers asyncio_atexit only after start() returns, and the caller never gets the instance. So the Chrome process keeps running after the interpreter exits (reparented to ppid 1, still alive 20 s later), the /tmp/uc_* profile is never removed, and the registry keeps the Browser. The only failure path that cleans up is the `if not self.info` branch, which calls self.stop().",
              "member_verdicts": [
