                "risks": "Because __dict__ is set to self, object.__getattribute__ would also return a key's value ahead of dict methods (functions are non-data descriptors, so the instance dict wins). A fix must therefore resolve the method names through dict/type (e.g. getattr(super(), name)) before the key lookup. Nothing internal relies on attrs.<method-name> returning the attribute value since d4d8117 switched Element.get to attrs.get()."
