          {
            "lens": "fixsafety",
            "entry": {
              "group_id": "Q8",
              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "ContraDict.__getattribute__ (zendriver/core/_contradict.py, first line of the method, `if attribute in self: return self[attribute]`) returns the stored value before it looks at the class. So a key named clear/items/get/keys/values/update/pop/copy hides the dict method, which contradicts the class docstring and the class's own warning message. Element._attrs is a ContraDict filled from DOM attributes, and Element.get_js_attributes() also returns one. Because of that, real pages with <br clear=all>, <x items=...> or <x get=...> make several calls raise TypeError: 'str' object is not callable. Affected calls: Element.update(), await elem, query_selector(_all), save_to_dom/remove_from_dom/set_value (via attrs.clear()); repr/str of the element or any ancestor, and Tab.get_all_urls (via attrs.items()); Element.get, elem[...] and elem.<x> (via attrs.get()); get_js_attributes().clear(). I reproduced all of this on the repo code, both browser-free and with real headless Chromium. A one-line local fix removes it.",
              "member_verdicts": [
