                }
              ],
              "evidence": "Pure probe on repo (zendriver from /home/user/zendriver/zendriver/__init__.py): `cd.items(): TypeError: 'str' object is not callable`, `cd.get('id'): TypeError`, `br.attrs.clear(): TypeError`, `repr(my-list): TypeError`, `str(div wrapping my-list): TypeError`, `span.get('id')/span['id']/span.id: TypeError`. Real headless Chromium on repo: `br attrs {'id': 'b', 'clear': 'all'}`, then `await br.update(): TypeError`, `br.query_selector('x'): TypeError`, `str(#wrap): TypeError`, `span.get('id'): TypeError`, `tab.get_all_urls(): TypeError`, `br.get_js_attributes().clear(): TypeError`. Same probe on the prototype: `await br.update(): OK -> '<br id=\"b\" clear=\"all\"></br>'`, `str(#wrap): OK -> '<div id=\"wrap\"><my-list items=\"[1,2]\"></my-list></div>'`, `span.get('id'): OK -> 's'`, `tab.get_all_urls(): OK -> ['http://x.example/a']`, `get_js_attributes().clear(): OK`. Regression test on repo: `4 failed, 3 passed`. On the prototype: `7 passed` (zendriver imported from .../Q8-fixsafety/pkg/zendriver/__init__.py). Repo suites test_tab, test_browser, test_cloudflare, test_frames and test_keyinputs (headless, not external) give `69 passed, 4 deselected` on both the prototype and an untouched copy. Scripts: /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/Q8-fixsafety/probe_pure.py and /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/Q8-fixsafety/probe_chrome.py.",
              "refinements": "Cited locations are accurate: ContraDict.__getattribute__ line 53; Element.update attrs.clear() at element.py:334; Element.__repr__ attrs.items() at 1160; Element.get at 239; Element.__getitem__ at 265; Tab.get_all_urls attrs.items() at tab.py:1629. More internal callers also reach the crash through Element.update(): Element.query_selector/query_selector_all (element.py ~825/834), Element.set_value (~784/788), Tab.query_selector(_all) with _node (tab.py ~584/657), Tab.find_elements_by_text when a text node has no parent (tab.py ~736), and the body.update() in tab.py ~1458. A key named `__class__` also broke ContraDict.__init__ itself (`ContraDict({'__class__':1,'x':{'a':1}})` raises TypeError 'int' object is not callable on the repo); the prototype fixes that too. The finder's pure-probe example `cd.copy().clear()` is not a valid repro: copy() returns a plain dict. Use cd.clear() on the ContraDict itself. Fix note: the obvious 'swap the two checks' fix (run _check_key before the key lookup) is NOT safe. It makes getattr(cd,'class'), getattr(cd,'data-id') and cd.Items raise AttributeError, as shown by probe_reorder.py. Use the hasattr(type(self), ...) guard instead.",
