            "lens": "fixsafety",
            "entry": {
              "group_id": "Q9",
              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "Both Browser.__aexit__ (zendriver/core/browser.py, Browser.__aexit__ ~l.837-841) and Connection.__aexit__ (zendriver/core/connection.py, Connection.__aexit__ ~l.593-599, which Tab inherits: zd.Tab.__aexit__ is Connection.__aexit__ is True) run `if exc_type and exc_val: raise exc_type(exc_val)`. That rebuilds whatever the block raised. Exceptions whose constructors need several arguments (JSONDecodeError, UnicodeDecodeError, websockets ConnectionClosedError, ExceptionGroup) come out as TypeError. ProtocolException comes back as a new instance with .code=None. KeyError('k') becomes KeyError(KeyError('k')). sys.exit(3) inside the block exits the process with status 1. The caught exception's traceback points into __aexit__, and the original survives only as __context__. The minimal fix is to stop rebuilding: return None and let Python re-raise the original. I prototyped it. My regression test fails 14 of 16 cases on the repo code and passes 16 of 16 on the prototype. mypy reports no new errors, and the repo's test_connection.py and test_browser.py pass on the prototype (19 passed).",
              "member_verdicts": [
                {
                  "fid": "A2.7",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Real headless Chromium, Python 3.13, repo code: `async with tab: await tab.send(cdp.dom.resolve_node(node_id=999999))` gives ProtocolException code=None. The prototype gives code=-32000. The same result came from a fake CDP peer returning error code -32000. Inside `async with conn`, UnicodeDecodeError, ConnectionClosedError(None, None) and a TaskGroup ExceptionGroup each turn into a TypeError ('function takes exactly 5 arguments (1 given)', \"ConnectionClosed.__init__() missing 1 required positional argument: 'sent'\", 'BaseExceptionGroup.__new__() takes exactly 2 arguments (1 given)'). KeyError('k') becomes KeyError(KeyError('k')). All of these pass on the prototype."
                },
