                  "fid": "A3.8",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Re-raise part confirmed on a Browser(Config(headless=True)) with no Chrome started: ConnectionClosedError and JSONDecodeError become TypeError, and ProtocolException({'code':-32000}) comes back with code=None. It also happens with a real `zd.start()` browser. The sub-claim that 'the browser is never stopped' is accurate: __aexit__ does nothing else, and in my real-Chrome probe the browser was still usable after the block. That is a separate design question, though: calling stop() in __aexit__ would change behaviour for existing users. The minimal fix leaves it alone."
