                  "note": "JSONDecodeError inside `async with browser`, `async with tab` (real Chrome) and `async with conn` (fake peer) gives TypeError(\"JSONDecodeError.__init__() missing 2 required positional arguments: 'doc' and 'pos'\"), so `except json.JSONDecodeError` misses it. A TaskGroup failure gives TypeError('BaseExceptionGroup.__new__() takes exactly 2 arguments (1 given)'). Both propagate unchanged on the prototype."
                }
              ],
              "evidence": "Regression test /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/Q9-fixsafety/test_q9_aexit.py (browser-free: a Browser instance with no Chrome, an in-process websockets fake CDP peer, plus a subprocess for sys.exit). Python 3.13.16.\n\nRepo run (no PYTHONPATH): 'zendriver imported from: /home/user/zendriver/zendriver/__init__.py' then '14 failed, 2 passed in 0.71s'. The 2 that pass are control tests: no exception, and asyncio.timeout around the block. Sample failures:\n- AssertionError: TypeError(\"JSONDecodeError.__init__() missing 2 required positional arguments: 'doc' and 'pos'\")\n- TypeError('BaseExceptionGroup.__new__() takes exactly 2 arguments (1 given)')\n- assert None == -32000, where None = ProtocolException(ProtocolException({'code': -32000, 'message': 'No node with given id found'})).code\n- sys.exit: AssertionError: (1, '3\\n')\n\nPrototype run (PYTHONPATH=<dir>/pkg): 'zendriver imported from: .../verify/Q9-fixsafety/pkg/zendriver/__init__.py' then '16 passed in 0.83s'.\n\nReal-Chromium probe (/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/Q9-fixsafety/probe_real.py):\n- repo: 'tab/protocol: ProtocolException code= None', 'tab/json: TypeError JSONDecodeError.__init__() missing 2...', 'browser/json: TypeError ...'\n- prototype: 'tab/protocol: ProtocolException code= -32000', 'tab/json: JSONDecodeError ...', 'browser/json: JSONDecodeError ...'\n\nThe repo's tests/core/test_connection.py and tests/core/test_browser.py, copied to scratch and run against the prototype with headless Chromium: '19 passed'.",
              "refinements": "1) The root cause is a single pattern in two methods: Browser.__aexit__ and Connection.__aexit__. Tab inherits Connection.__aexit__, so one fix covers `async with tab`. Exceptions whose type survives (KeyboardInterrupt, CancelledError, single-argument errors) still lose their attributes and traceback; with CancelledError, asyncio.timeout still works on both versions (control test passes). 2) A3.8's 'browser is never stopped' is a separate design/API issue (should `async with browser` call stop()?). It is not part of this root cause, and the minimal fix should not change it. 3) Side observation, not in this group: when writing the fake peer I found that a reply whose 'result' cannot be parsed (e.g. Target.getTargets answered with {}) leaves conn.send() hanging forever. Transaction.__call__ raises KeyError from the cdp parser instead of calling set_exception, so the future never completes. Worth checking whether another group already owns it. 4) Regression test portability: the ExceptionGroup/TaskGroup and asyncio.timeout cases need Python 3.11+. The project supports 3.10, so guard those cases with a version skip when upstreaming.",
              "chrome_claims": [
                {
                  "claim": "`async with tab:` around a failing DOM.resolveNode loses ProtocolException.code on repo code and keeps it (-32000) with the fix",
