                  "how": "Same probe_real.py run against real Chromium, repo and prototype"
                },
                {
                  "claim": "Browser stays running and usable after leaving `async with browser:`",
                  "status": "verified",
                  "how": "probe_real.py opened a new tab and evaluated 1+1 after the block exited, on both copies"
                }
              ],
              "realism": "high",
              "severity": "wrong-result",
              "fix_assessment": {
                "kind": "minimal-local",
                "prototype_dir": "/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/Q9-fixsafety/pkg",
                "diff_summary": "browser.py Browser.__aexit__: replace `if exc_type and exc_val: raise exc_type(exc_val)` with a comment and `return None`. connection.py Connection.__aexit__: keep `await self.aclose()` and delete the two re-raise lines; also widen the annotation to `exc_type: type[BaseException] | None`. ruff format and ruff check are clean.",
                "regression_test_path": "/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/Q9-fixsafety/test_q9_aexit.py",
                "fails_on_repo": "yes",
                "passes_on_prototype": "yes",
                "mypy_ok": "yes",
                "risks": "Very low. No locks are added, so there is no re-entrancy, deadlock or lock-ordering concern. Error and cancel paths: if aclose() raises or is cancelled inside Connection.__aexit__, that exception propagates with the original as __context__, the same as before (aclose already ran before the old re-raise line). Behaviour changes callers would notice: the original exception object, type, attributes and traceback now propagate. Code that, against intent, caught TypeError or relied on the double-wrapped args (e.g. KeyError(KeyError('k')).args) would see the real exception. sys.exit codes are now honoured. Tracebacks lose the 'During handling of the above exception' chain. mypy: 332 errors on both the prototype and an untouched copy, with an identical diff, so no new errors. Test portability: the ExceptionGroup and asyncio.timeout cases need a Python 3.11+ guard for the project's 3.10 support."
              }
            }
          }
        ]
