          {
            "lens": "fixsafety",
            "entry": {
              "group_id": "Q10",
              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "Tab.__call__(self, text=None, selector=None, timeout=10) at zendriver/core/tab.py:1966 returns `await self.wait_for(text, selector, timeout)`, passing its arguments by position. The signature is Tab.wait_for(self, selector=None, text=None, timeout=10) (tab.py:1284), so the two arguments land in each other's slots. tab(text=X) and tab(X) run query_selector(X) as CSS. If X is not a valid selector this fails at once, and otherwise it polls until the timeout. tab(selector=S) runs find_element_by_text(S). It works only because DOM.performSearch also accepts CSS. I reproduced this on real headless Chromium and fixed it in a one-line prototype: `return await self.wait_for(selector=selector, text=text, timeout=timeout)`.",
              "member_verdicts": [
                {
