              "evidence": "Code (read fresh): Tab.__call__ at tab.py:1952-1966 has signature (text, selector, timeout) and body `return await self.wait_for(text, selector, timeout)`. Tab.wait_for at tab.py:1284 has signature (selector, text, timeout) and checks `if selector:` (query_selector) before `if text:` (find_element_by_text). The swap was already present before dd9a4f8 (mypy strict PR, #182, which added the await, per git log -S); it is likely inherited from nodriver. No test in tests/ calls Tab.__call__.\n\nReal-Chromium probe (Python 3.13, websockets 14.1), page `<ul><li>Apples</li><li>Pears</li></ul><p id='p1'>Hello needle world</p><button>Sign up!</button>`:\nREPO (zendriver: /home/user/zendriver/zendriver/__init__.py):\n  tab(text='Hello needle'): EXC 2.02s -> TimeoutError: time ran out while waiting\n  tab('Hello needle') positional: EXC 2.02s -> TimeoutError\n  tab(text='Sign up!'): EXC 0.00s -> ProtocolException: DOM Error while querying ... selector: 'Sign up!'\n  tab(selector='#p1'): OK -> p ; tab(selector='li'): OK -> li 'Apples'\n  wait_for(text='Hello needle'): OK 0.00s -> p\nPROTOTYPE (zendriver: .../verify/Q10-fixsafety/pkg/zendriver/__init__.py): every case OK. text= finds the <p>, 'Sign up!' finds the <button>, and the selector= cases are unchanged.\n\nRegression test /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/Q10-fixsafety/test_q10_call_args.py has 4 browser-free tests (a never-connected Tab whose query_selector, find_element_by_text and sleep are patched on the instance; the real __call__ and wait_for run) and 1 real-Chromium test. Repo run: `zendriver imported from: /home/user/zendriver/zendriver/__init__.py` ... `4 failed, 1 passed in 5.37s`. The failures were text kwarg, selector kwarg, positional text and real chromium, all TimeoutError. The test that passed checks that a timeout is still raised. Prototype run (PYTHONPATH=pkg): `zendriver imported from: .../Q10-fixsafety/pkg/zendriver/__init__.py` ... `5 passed in 1.47s`.",
              "refinements": "1) Severity is wrong-result for all members. A12.1's 'crash' is overstated, though the ProtocolException path is real: text that is an invalid CSS selector fails at once with ProtocolException instead of TimeoutError. 2) tab(selector=...) is not fully OK on repo code either. It runs a text search, so a selector string that also appears as page text, or a selector performSearch handles differently, can return a different element than query_selector would. It also skips the CSS path's stale-document retry. 3) The docstring ('alias to query_selector_all or find_elements_by_text') is inaccurate: the method waits for and returns a single Element. Fixing it is optional and cosmetic. 4) Be careful with data: URLs in tests: a '#' in the HTML truncates the page as a URL fragment. My first positional probe was invalidated by this and rerun without '#'.",
