            "lens": "reproduce",
            "entry": {
              "group_id": "R13",
              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "Confirmed on real headless Chromium (Python 3.13.16, repo HEAD 064148f). The whole group comes from one problem: Element.get_position (element.py:519) is typed as returning `Position | None`, but it never returns None. (1) When DOM.getContentQuads returns [], which happens for display:none, for a button nested in a display:none parent, for a hidden file input and for a detached node, it runs `raise Exception('could not find position ...')` at line 529. The `except IndexError: return None` at the end can never fire, because quads[0] only runs when the list is non-empty. (2) When the element has no tree, the guard `not self.parent` at line 520 calls the parent property, which raises RuntimeError('could not get parent since the element has no tree set') at line 367. As a result, click() (line 418) fails inside its cosmetic `await self.flash(0.25)` at line 432 and never sends the JS `el.click()`. Calling apply('(el)=>el.click()') directly on the same element does work. The `if not position: warn; return` branches in mouse_click, mouse_move, mouse_drag and flash are dead code, and screenshot_b64 raises a plain Exception instead of the RuntimeError its docstring promises.",
              "member_verdicts": [
                {
                  "fid": "A8.3",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "`hid=await tab.select('#hid')` (display:none). The raw DOM.getContentQuads call returns []. hid.click() raised builtins.Exception 'could not find position for <button id=\"hid\" ...>'. The traceback runs click line 432 -> flash line 940 -> get_position line 529. window.hidClicked was None after the click. hid.apply('(el) => el.click()') then set window.hidClicked = 1, so a JS click works on the hidden element. A detached node gives the same result: getContentQuads returns [], not a ProtocolException, click() raises, and apply(el.click) works."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "B15.6",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "The same run shows click() raising the same bare Exception for a nested display:none button and a hidden <input type=file>, with nestedClicked and fileClicked both None. On #hid, get_position, mouse_click, mouse_move, mouse_drag((10,10)), vis.mouse_drag(hid) (through destination.get_position), flash and screenshot_b64 all raised builtins.Exception rather than logging a warning and returning. For screenshot_b64, isinstance(e, RuntimeError) was False, despite the docstring. Control cases: a visible button and a visibility:hidden button both click fine, because they have quads."
                },
                {
