              "evidence": "Commands: `export PATH=/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/bin:$PATH; cd /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/R13-reproduce/ && timeout 120 /home/user/zendriver/.venv/bin/python probe_hidden.py` and the same for probe_extra.py. zendriver was imported from /home/user/zendriver/zendriver/__init__.py on python 3.13.16. Key lines: 'raw DOM.getContentQuads for #hid -> []'; '[hid click] EXC builtins.Exception: could not find position for <button id=\"hid\" style=\"display:none\" ...>' with the traceback click:432 -> flash:940 -> get_position:529; 'window.hidClicked after click() = None'; '[hid apply el.click()] OK' and 'window.hidClicked after apply(el.click) = 1'; '[hid mouse_click (should warn+return)] EXC builtins.Exception ...' (the same for mouse_move, mouse_drag, flash and screenshot_b64); 'screenshot_b64 exception is RuntimeError? False'; 'lnk tree: None'; '[lnk click 1] EXC builtins.RuntimeError: could not get parent since the element has no tree set' with the traceback get_position:520 -> parent:367; 'window.lnkClicks after click 1 = None'; '[lnk2 mouse_click 1 (fresh)] OK' then '[lnk2 mouse_click 2] EXC builtins.RuntimeError'; '[lnk3 click after update()] OK' and 'lnkClicks = 2'; '[detached click] EXC builtins.Exception: could not find position' and 'detClicked after apply = 1'; '[visibility:hidden click] OK, vhClicked = 1'. Outputs are saved in probe_hidden.out and probe_extra.out in the scratch dir. Both browsers were stopped with browser.stop(), the temp dirs were removed, and no chromium processes were left.",
              "refinements": "For a detached node, getContentQuads in this Chromium returns [] rather than a 'Could not compute content quads' ProtocolException, so it takes the same raise-Exception path. Hiding the element with visibility:hidden does not trigger the bug, because quads exist. screenshot_b64 on a tree-less element does raise a RuntimeError, but it is the parent-property RuntimeError, not the documented one. Every other R13 path raises a bare Exception. get_position's only callers are in element.py, and no repo test covers hidden elements. A fix needs two parts: return None when quads are empty, and do not call `self.parent` in the guard. A tree-less element should simply re-resolve the node.",
