              "evidence": "Scripts I wrote and ran myself, under `timeout 120`, with headless Chromium on PATH, from the scratch dir; each printed zendriver.__file__ = /home/user/zendriver/zendriver/__init__.py on Python 3.13.16. (1) /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/R13-refute/probe_hidden.py printed '[raw quads] dn: []', and the same for parentdn, file, hiddeninp, indetails, hattr and detached. It also printed '[raw quads] vhid/op0/cb/zero: [Quad(...)]', '[click] dn: EXC Exception: could not find position for <button id=\"dn\" ...; js-click-counter=None', '[apply click] dn counter: 1', and '[mouse_click|mouse_move|mouse_drag|screenshot_b64|flash|get_position] dn: EXC Exception: could not find position'. (2) /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/R13-refute/probe_treeless.py printed 'tree is None: True', '[linked lnk.click #1] EXC RuntimeError: could not get parent since the element has no tree set; counter=None', '[fresh linked lnk.mouse_click #1] ok; counter=1', '[same lnk.mouse_click #2] EXC RuntimeError ...', '[updated lnk.click] ok; counter=2', and showed tree set for find, select_all, find_all, xpath and children. (3) /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/R13-refute/probe_more.py printed '[raw quads] opt: []', '[click] opt: EXC Exception ...', '[click] dc (display:contents): ok', and confirmed that tab.find('hidden menu item') returns the display:none <li>. I also downloaded upstream sources into /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/R13-refute/upstream/. nodriver's flash() has `try: pos = await self.get_position() except (Exception,): logger.debug(...); return`. zendriver main's get_position and click are identical to the local copy, and its flash has the same `if pos is None` handling. Every browser I started was stopped with browser.stop(), and the temp page dirs were removed.",
              "refinements": "Only elements with no layout box trigger the click() failure: display:none on the element or an ancestor, the hidden attribute, input type=hidden, a closed <details>, <option> in a closed <select>, and detached nodes. Elements that are visually hidden but still laid out (visibility:hidden, opacity:0, clip-based visually-hidden, 0x0, display:contents) click fine. The RuntimeError path needs a tree-less Element, and the only built-in source is Tab.get_all_linked_sources(). mouse_click() on such an element works once, then fails once _remote_object is set. Not Python-version dependent. Fix caution: if get_position returns None, mouse_click, mouse_move and mouse_drag become silent no-ops (warn and return) on hidden elements. That arguably hides failures, so a fix may prefer catching the error in flash() only, as nodriver does, or keep mouse_* raising. screenshot_b64 should raise its documented RuntimeError. Avoid self.parent in the guard (check self._remote_object / object_id only) so tree-less elements work.",
