          {
            "lens": "fixsafety",
            "entry": {
              "group_id": "R13",
              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "Confirmed on real headless Chromium 141 (Python 3.13). For display:none elements and for detached or removed nodes, DOM.getContentQuads returns []. Element.get_position (zendriver/core/element.py, get_position ~l.519-544) then runs `if not quads: raise Exception('could not find position ...')`, so its `except IndexError: return None` never fires, even though the method is annotated `-> Position | None`. click() calls the cosmetic flash(0.25) before the JS el.click(), so it raises and the JS click is never sent. The `if not position` branches in mouse_click, mouse_move, mouse_drag and flash are dead code, and screenshot_b64 raises a plain Exception instead of the RuntimeError its docstring promises. Separately, the guard `not self.parent` in get_position raises RuntimeError for tree-less Elements (Tab.get_all_linked_sources builds them with element.create(asset.node, self)) as soon as _remote_object is cached. So click() always fails on them, and every mouse_click after the first one fails too.",
              "member_verdicts": [
                {
                  "fid": "A8.3",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Real Chromium, repo code: `await (await tab.query_selector('#hid')).click()` on <button style=display:none onclick=...> raises Exception 'could not find position for <button id=\"hid\" ...>' and window.hidClicked stays None. Raw DOM.getContentQuads returned []. A detached node created with createElement also returned [] (no ProtocolException). With the prototype fix, click() runs the JS click and hidClicked == 1."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "B15.6",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Same root cause. On repo code, get_position, click, mouse_click, mouse_move, flash and screenshot_b64 on the display:none button all raised a bare Exception. A hidden <input type=file> click also raised, and fileClicked stayed None. screenshot_b64 raised Exception, not the documented RuntimeError. With the prototype: mouse_click and mouse_move log their 'could not find location ..., not clicking/moving' warning and return, flash warns and returns, and screenshot_b64 raises RuntimeError('could not determine position ...')."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "A8.4",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Real Chromium, repo code: a link from tab.get_all_linked_sources() has tree None. click() #1 and #2 both raise RuntimeError('could not get parent since the element has no tree set'), and window.lnkClicks stays None. On a fresh tree-less element the first mouse_click() works (the `not self._remote_object` short-circuit skips self.parent). The second mouse_click() and a later get_position() raise RuntimeError. With the prototype, both clicks and both mouse_clicks work, and lnkClicks counts them."
                }
              ],
              "evidence": "Real Chromium probe /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/R13-fixsafety/probe_real.py, repo code (zendriver from /home/user/zendriver/zendriver/__init__.py, python 3.13.16):\n[raw quads display:none] []\n[click hidden] EXC Exception: could not find position for <button id=\"hid\" style=\"display:none\" ...>\n   window.hidClicked = None\n[screenshot_b64 hidden] EXC Exception: could not find position ...\n[lnk tree] None\n[lnk click 1] EXC RuntimeError: could not get parent since the element has no tree set\n[lnk2 mouse_click 1] OK -> None\n[lnk2 mouse_click 2] EXC RuntimeError: could not get parent since the element has no tree set\n[raw quads detached] []\nSame probe on the prototype (pkg copy): click hidden OK, hidClicked = 1; screenshot_b64 hidden raises RuntimeError; lnk clicks OK, lnkClicks = 2.\n\nBrowser-free regression test test_r13_position.py (fake Tab that drives the cdp generators):\n- repo: 'zendriver imported from: /home/user/zendriver/zendriver/__init__.py' ... '7 failed, 1 passed in 0.35s' (the 1 pass is the unchanged visible-element control test)\n- prototype: 'zendriver imported from: .../R13-fixsafety/pkg/zendriver/__init__.py' ... '8 passed in 0.23s'\n\nReal-Chromium regression test test_r13_chromium.py:\n- repo: '2 failed, 1 passed in 2.88s' (Exception could not find position / RuntimeError could not get parent; the control test passes)\n- prototype: '3 passed in 3.43s'\n\nExisting repo tests (copied to scratch; test_tab, test_mouse, test_frames, test_cloudflare, -m 'not external', headless): '55 passed, 4 deselected' on both the untouched copy and the prototype, with the copy's path printed inside pytest.\n\nmypy (uv run --no-sync mypy --config-file pyproject.toml <copy>/zendriver): the output of the untouched copy and the prototype is identical after path normalisation, so no new errors and 0 errors in core/element.py.",
              "refinements": "1) cloudflare.py verify_cf (~l.263) string-matches 'could not find position' on an exception from Tab.mouse_click(x, y). That coordinate-based call never goes through Element.get_position, so the branch is already dead and the fix does not change it. It will just stay dead (could be cleaned up separately). 2) The `not self.parent` guard checks only the cached tree, so it never detected staleness. It only added an O(tree) walk and Element allocation on every get_position call, and broke tree-less elements. Dropping it is safe. 3) Side observation, not in this group: the red dot from flash() has no pointer-events:none and sits at the element's centre for its duration. A mouse_click() right after click() (within 0.25-0.5 s) lands on the dot instead of the element. My Chromium test needed a 0.6 s sleep for that reason.",
              "chrome_claims": [
                {
                  "claim": "DOM.getContentQuads returns an empty quads list (not a ProtocolException) for a display:none element",
                  "status": "verified",
                  "how": "Raw tab.send(cdp.dom.get_content_quads(...)) on Chromium 141 headless printed []"
                },
                {
                  "claim": "DOM.getContentQuads returns [] for a detached node and for an element removed from the DOM after its remote object was resolved",
                  "status": "verified",
                  "how": "Probe: createElement node gave [] directly; get_position on a removed #vis returned None on the prototype"
                },
                {
                  "claim": "JS el.click() on a display:none element fires its onclick handler",
                  "status": "verified",
                  "how": "Prototype click() on #hid set window.hidClicked=1; also the hidden file input set fileClicked=1"
                },
                {
                  "claim": "visibility:hidden elements still have content quads (not affected by this bug)",
                  "status": "verified",
                  "how": "get_position on button inside visibility:hidden span returned a Position on repo code"
                }
              ],
              "realism": "high",
              "severity": "crash",
              "fix_assessment": {
                "kind": "minimal-local",
                "prototype_dir": "/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/R13-fixsafety/pkg",
                "diff_summary": "zendriver/core/element.py Element.get_position: (a) `if not self._remote_object or not self.parent or not self.object_id:` becomes `if not self._remote_object or not self.object_id:`; (b) delete `if not quads: raise Exception(\"could not find position for %s \" % self)`, so an empty quads list hits `quads[0]`, and the existing `except IndexError` logs at debug and returns None as intended. An explicit variant with the same behaviour is `if not quads: logger.debug(...); return None` plus dropping the try/except IndexError. Full diff: /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/R13-fixsafety/fix.diff",
                "regression_test_path": "/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/R13-fixsafety/test_r13_position.py (browser-free, fake Tab); /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/R13-fixsafety/test_r13_chromium.py (real Chromium)",
                "fails_on_repo": "yes",
                "passes_on_prototype": "yes",
                "mypy_ok": "yes",
                "risks": "No locks, tasks or cancellation are involved, so there is no re-entrancy, deadlock or lock-ordering risk. Error paths: ProtocolExceptions from resolveNode or getContentQuads (stale ids after navigation) still propagate as before. Behaviour changes callers would notice: (1) click() on a display:none, detached or removed element now sends the JS el.click() and returns instead of raising. On a removed node the handler still fires: verified, visClicked went from 1 to 2 on a removed button, and no exception is raised. Code that used click() raising as an implicit 'element gone or hidden' check now passes silently. (2) Each such click() logs a WARNING 'flash() : could not determine position'; a maintainer might want this at debug level. (3) mouse_click, mouse_move and mouse_drag on hidden elements now warn and return (a silent no-op) instead of raising. This is the documented intent, but failures become less visible. (4) screenshot_b64 and save_screenshot raise RuntimeError instead of a bare Exception; RuntimeError subclasses Exception, so `except Exception` still works. (5) get_position() returns None instead of raising, which matches its existing Optional annotation. (6) Tree'd elements whose parent is not in the cached tree now reuse the cached remote object instead of calling DOM.resolveNode on every call, with fewer round-trips and no full-tree walk. The behaviour does not depend on the Python version (ran on 3.13)."
              }
            }
          }
        ]
