                }
              ],
              "evidence": "Commands, run from /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/R14-reproduce with the repo copy imported (zendriver from /home/user/zendriver/zendriver/__init__.py, py 3.13.16):\n1) TMPDIR=$PWD/tmp1 timeout 60 .venv/bin/python p1_repr.py -> '[repr] before: _user_data_dir=None custom=False' / '[repr] after : _user_data_dir=.../uc_mjq1sky0 custom=False' / '[repr] deepcopies share path: True'; the same for str, call and attr; '[control] deepcopies distinct: True'.\n2) TMPDIR=$PWD/tmp2 timeout 120 .venv/bin/python p2_leak.py -> 'after 3 bad-exe starts: [uc_a_jbdoyb, uc_k_fxkixw, uc_v2rlnuak]'; 'instance udd materialized at __init__? .../uc_5o734t8d'; 'after stop(): dir exists? True'; 'connect-existing failed: Exception Failed to connect to browser'; 'new after connect-existing failure: [uc_t4sxesfa]'.\n3) PATH=<scratchpad>/bin:$PATH timeout 150 .venv/bin/python p3_shared.py control -> b1 and b2 started with distinct udds, 'same udd: False', b1 profile kept after b2.stop.\n4) ... p3_shared.py repr -> 'b2: start FAILED: Exception: Failed to connect to browser' / 'b1 still running: True  b1 profile exists: False'.\n5) ... p4_who_rmtree.py (config() on the template, shutil.rmtree spy) -> b2 stderr 'process_singleton_posix.cc:340 Failed to create .../uc_25duiqyk/SingletonLock: File exists (17) ... Aborting now to avoid profile corruption'; 'RMTREE uc_25duiqyk via [... start:594, stop:872, _stop:919, _cleanup_temporary_profile:927]'; 'b1 alive: True b1 profile exists: False'.\nIntended behavior: the Config.__init__ comment says the temp dir is deferred 'so config can be used/reused as a template for multiple browser instances', and tests/core/test_multiple_browsers.py asserts unique udds from one template. All browsers I started were stopped or killed (no leftover processes) and the tmp1-3 dirs were removed.",
              "refinements": "Two separate mechanisms are involved. (1) Template sharing: the user's own repr(), str() or config() call, or the user_data_dir getter, on the template materializes the lazy dir. Browser.__init__'s debug log does NOT touch the template, because it formats vars(self) after the deepcopy, so only user-side inspection triggers the sharing bug. (2) Leak: the eager '%' formatting in Browser.__init__ (~L274) materializes the per-instance copy's dir, and _stop's early return (~L875) skips _cleanup_temporary_profile when start() failed before a process or connection existed. On the connect-existing path, a temp profile is created even though it is never used. In my runs b2's Chromium aborted on SingletonLock 'File exists' and did not hand off to b1's process. The scratch TMPDIR is long, which may affect the singleton socket path. Either way b2 fails and its stop() deletes the shared dir. The leaked dirs are empty mkdtemp dirs, one per failed attempt.",
