        "lenses": [
          {
            "lens": "reproduce",
            "entry": {
              "group_id": "R15",
              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "All five config-argument claims reproduce on Python 3.13.16 against the repo copy, with my own probes. The worst one is K5. Config.add_argument rejects any argument whose lowercased text contains headless, lang, data-dir, data_dir, no-sandbox or no_sandbox. Browser.start passes --load-extension through add_argument, so Browser.create raises ValueError, and the browser never starts, whenever an extension path contains one of those substrings (for example .../headless-scraper/ext or /opt/LanguageTool). K2: argv carries duplicate copies of flags that Config adds itself (confirmed in /proc/<pid>/cmdline of a real Chromium). When the values differ, Config's copy comes last and silently overrides the user's browser_args value, because Chrome uses the last value of a repeated switch. K4: Config stores the caller's non-empty list by reference, so add_argument mutates it and leaks into other Configs built from the same list. K1: the browser_args property returns sorted(defaults + user args). It does not merge --disable-features and does not dedupe, so it differs from Config(). K3: each start() appends another --load-extension to browser.config. On an ordinary restart the duplicates never reach a launched Chromium, because start() keeps the host/port it set and takes the connect_existing path; they reach the real argv only if host/port are cleared by hand.",
              "member_verdicts": [
                {
                  "fid": "SEED-K1",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "With Config(browser_args=['--disable-features=Foo','--no-first-run','--mute-audio','--mute-audio']), the property shows two separate --disable-features entries and two copies each of --no-first-run and --mute-audio. Config() returns one merged --disable-features and only one --no-first-run. The property also leaves out --user-data-dir, --no-sandbox and the webrtc flags. Within the library, only Config.__repr__ reads it, so the impact is cosmetic: it only misleads someone inspecting the config. Related: the property has no setter, so `config.browser_args = [...]`, which docs/quickstart.md shows, raises AttributeError (docs are out of scope)."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "SEED-K2",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Without a browser, Config() returned 2 copies each of --headless=new, --no-sandbox, --lang=de-DE, --disable-webgl, --disable-webgl2, both webrtc flags and --user-agent=UA. In real Chromium, /proc/<pid>/cmdline held 2x --headless=new and 2x --no-sandbox, plus conflicting pairs ['--lang=fr-FR','--lang=de-DE'] and ['--webrtc-ip-handling-policy=default_public_interface_only','--webrtc-ip-handling-policy=disable_non_proxied_udp']. To check what Chrome does with a repeated switch, I passed browser_args=['--user-agent=FromBrowserArgs/1.0'] with user_agent='FromConfigAttr/1.0'; Browser.getVersion reported 'FromConfigAttr/1.0', so the last copy wins. Identical duplicates are therefore harmless. The real effect is that Config's appended flags (including the default disable_webrtc=True) silently override what the user set in browser_args. __call__ only dedupes user args against the defaults and --user-data-dir, not against the user list itself or the flags appended later."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "SEED-K3",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Real Chromium, Config with add_extension(ext/plain). The 1st start has one --load-extension. After stop() and start() on the same instance, browser.config._browser_args and browser.config() hold 2 copies, but that 2nd start raised ConnectionRefusedError: host/port are still set on the config, so it takes the connect_existing path and launches no process. After clearing host and port by hand, a 3rd start launched Chromium with 3 identical --load-extension entries in its real argv. Browser.__init__ deepcopies the config, so a fresh Browser.create(cfg) that reuses the caller's Config sees only 1 copy. Since Chrome uses the last value and the copies are identical, the effect is cosmetic."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "SEED-K4",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "mine=['--window-size=800,600']; c=Config(browser_args=mine): c._browser_args is mine is True. After c.add_argument('--mute-audio'), mine == ['--window-size=800,600','--mute-audio'], and a second Config(browser_args=mine) also emits --mute-audio. An empty list is not aliased, because `if not browser_args` swaps in a fresh []. This only bites when the user calls Config directly: zendriver.start and Browser.create deepcopy the Config, so the add_argument inside Browser.start never touches the caller's list."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "SEED-K5",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "add_argument raised ValueError for --disable-features=LanguageDetectionAPI, --accept-lang=fr-FR, --enable-features=TranslateUI,LanguageSettings, --load-extension=/home/me/headless-scraper/ext, --load-extension=/opt/LanguageTool and --disk-cache-dir=/tmp/user-data-dir-cache, and accepted --mute-audio. The error message says to use a Config attribute, but none exists for these. End to end: Config.add_extension('<scratch>/ext/headless-scraper/ext') followed by Browser.create(cfg) raised ValueError from Browser.start's internal add_argument('--load-extension=...'). No browser was launched, so a legitimate extension cannot be used from such a path. Passing the same flags through the browser_args constructor argument skips validation entirely, which is inconsistent."
                }
              ],
              "evidence": "Python 3.13.16; every probe printed zendriver.__file__ = /home/user/zendriver/zendriver/__init__.py.\n\n(1) cd /tmp && timeout 120 /home/user/zendriver/.venv/bin/python /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/R15-reproduce/probe_config.py\nKey lines:\n- \"property --disable-features entries: ['--disable-features=Foo', '--disable-features=IsolateOrigins,...']\" vs \"call() ... ['--disable-features=IsolateOrigins,DisableLoadExtensionCommandLineSwitch,site-per-process,Foo']\"\n- \"property duplicates: {'--mute-audio': 2, '--no-first-run': 2}\"\n- \"duplicates in Config(): {'--headless=new': 2, '--no-sandbox': 2, '--lang=de-DE': 2, '--disable-webgl': 2, ...}\"\n- \"c._browser_args is mine: True\"; \"caller list after c.add_argument: ['--window-size=800,600', '--mute-audio']\"\n- \"REJECTED --disable-features=LanguageDetectionAPI\", \"REJECTED --load-extension=/home/me/headless-scraper/ext\"\n\n(2) cd /tmp && PATH=<scratchpad>/bin:$PATH timeout 150 /home/user/zendriver/.venv/bin/python .../R15-reproduce/probe_browser.py (real headless Chromium, explicit user_data_dir under scratch)\nKey lines:\n- \"duplicates in real argv: {'--headless=new': 2, '--no-sandbox': 2}\"\n- \"webrtc entries in argv: ['--webrtc-ip-handling-policy=default_public_interface_only', '--webrtc-ip-handling-policy=disable_non_proxied_udp']\"\n- \"2nd start (same instance) raised: ConnectionRefusedError\"\n- \"after 2nd start: browser.config._browser_args: [--load-extension=... x2]\"\n- \"3rd start (host/port cleared): load-extension in real argv: [x3]\"\n- \"new Browser.create(cfg) reusing caller cfg: [x1]\"\n- \"Browser.create raised ValueError: \\\"--load-extension=.../ext/headless-scraper/ext\\\" not allowed\"\n\n(3) .../R15-reproduce/probe_lastwins.py\nKey lines:\n- \"argv user-agent entries: ['--user-agent=FromBrowserArgs/1.0', '--user-agent=FromConfigAttr/1.0']\"\n- \"Browser.getVersion userAgent: FromConfigAttr/1.0\"\n\nCode references: Config.__init__ sets self._browser_args = browser_args (config.py ~l.92). browser_args property (~l.136). __call__ dedupes only against the defaults (~l.204) and returns merge_disable_features_args. add_argument does a substring check (~l.229-245). Browser.start calls self.config.add_argument('--load-extension=...') (browser.py ~l.558), after host/port are set (~l.531-535).\n\nCleanup: every browser I started was stopped (pgrep showed none left), and scratch profiles/ and tmp/ were removed. probe_config.py also created 7 empty temp profile dirs in /tmp before I redirected TMPDIR (/tmp/uc_o4lvh6pz, /tmp/uc_0os3juwr, /tmp/uc_561nf5mr, /tmp/uc_c9kjatqh, /tmp/uc_jpi9md2j, /tmp/uc_usq0znzt, /tmp/uc_v52qt7g_). Removing them was denied by the permission classifier, so they remain. The repo is unmodified (git status clean).",
              "refinements": "K3: the duplicates never reach a launched Chromium on an ordinary restart. After stop(), start() reuses the host/port it assigned and takes the connect_existing path, which fails with ConnectionRefusedError (that is a separate restart issue). The start() branch for a process that has exited (create(config=self.config)) also keeps host/port, so it takes the same path. K2: identical duplicates are harmless because Chrome uses the last value. The defect worth fixing is precedence: Config-appended flags (user_agent, lang, the default disable_webrtc=True policy, headless) override conflicting values the user put in browser_args. Also, browser_args=['--headless=new'] with headless=False leaves config.headless False, so the headless UA patch in start() is skipped. K5 is the member with real user impact: Browser.start aborts with ValueError for any extension directory whose path contains a blocked substring, and the substring list also blocks unrelated flags such as --accept-lang and *Language* feature names. A fix should match flag names exactly (split on '=' and compare the switch name) and should not route the internal --load-extension through the user-facing validation. K1: the only internal consumer is __repr__. K4: aliasing only shows when Config is used directly, since Browser deepcopies.",
              "chrome_claims": [
                {
                  "claim": "Real Chromium receives duplicate --headless=new and --no-sandbox, and conflicting --lang/--webrtc-ip-handling-policy pairs, in its argv",
                  "status": "verified",
                  "how": "read /proc/<pid>/cmdline of the Chromium launched by zendriver.start in probe_browser.py"
                },
