              "evidence": "All scripts are in /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/R16-refute/ and were run with the repo copy imported (zendriver.__file__=/home/user/zendriver/zendriver/__init__.py), Python 3.13.16, websockets 14.1, Chromium 141.0.7390.37, each under `timeout`.\n\nfake_probes.py (in-process websockets server):\n- C1: 'conn.websocket is None: False conn.closed: False', 'send #0..2: raised ConnectionClosedError: received 1011', 'server saw connections: 1', 'after aclose()+send(): server connections: 2'.\n- C2: 'aclose() returned; websocket is None: True', 'pending send after aclose(): SUCCEEDED', 'listener running: True server open sockets: 1'.\n- C3: 'mapper size after 5 timed-out never-answered sends: 5 [(2, True)...]', 'mapper size after aclose(): 0'.\n\nc1_chrome_probe.py: 'browser send raised ConnectionClosedError sent 1009', 'chrome process alive: True', 'fresh Connection to same URL works', 'after manual websocket=None: browser send ok', 'tab.evaluate -> 2'.\n\nc3_chrome_probe.py: '200 entries; ~1282 bytes/entry', 'mapper size 1s after navigating the page: 0', 'mapper size 1s after reload: 0'.\n\nwait_probe.py: control 'finished after 1.11s'; cases A, B, D and E 'STILL PENDING after ~8.3s -> HANG' with the stack at 'connection.py, line 579, in wait: await self.listener.idle.wait()'; case C (close after 50 ms) HANG; case C2 (300 ms) finished.\n\nsweep_probe.py: 'delay 0 ms: raise; 20/40/60/80 ms: HANG HANG; 100-250 ms: ok ok'.\n\npopup_probe.py: 'hangs: 0/6' (raised 'target session was detached').\n\ntabget_probe.py: 'Tab.get STILL PENDING 6s after the tab closed -> HANG' at tab.py:513.\n\nHistory: `await self.listener.idle.wait()` and the `websocket is None` check in aopen both come from the initial import (5c1a005), not from a deliberate change. CHANGELOG entry #285 ('Fix commands hanging forever when the browser connection closed...') shows the project treats hangs-on-close as bugs. No test asserts the current wait() or no-reconnect behaviour.",
              "refinements": "B14.5:\n- It hangs only if the tab's session listener is busy (idle clear) when the session detaches.\n- On a quiet page with no domains enabled, the window is only about the listener's time_before_considered_idle (0.1 s; 0.75 s in interactive mode) after the last session message. wait()'s own Target.getTargetInfo reply counts as such a message, so the window measured 20-80 ms after the call.\n- A close that lands before the getTargetInfo reply makes wait() raise ProtocolException instead of hanging. That is the case for an immediate click-to-window.close().\n- On pages with a steady stream of events (handlers or manually enabled Network/Runtime/Page domains), the window covers the whole wait.\n- Affected: wait() with t=None, `await tab`, Tab.get(url) on the same tab (tab.py:513), and get/set_local_storage when target.url is empty.\n- Not affected: wait(t) with a number (it uses wait_for), and Browser.get.\n- Triggers: Target.closeTarget, tab.close() from another task, page window.close(), browser.stop() from another task, and a Chrome crash or kill.\n- Nothing else ends the wait: websockets keepalive does not touch the Event, and a new Listener created later has a new Event.\n- Not specific to a Python version (the Event is simply never set).\n\nSEED-C1:\n- Severity is wrong-result/cosmetic, not hang. The connection is permanently dead and `closed` reports False, but later sends raise at once.\n- It matters only when Chrome survives the socket close.\n\nSEED-C2:\n- Only reachable through a direct Connection.aclose() during the first or re-opening aopen. Browser.stop does not trigger it (stop skips aclose when closed is True), and the process kill bounds it for local browsers.\n\nSEED-C3:\n- The entry lives only until Chrome replies, the session detaches or the connection closes. Chrome replies to pending awaitPromise evaluates on navigation or reload.\n- Only commands that are never answered accumulate, at about 1.3 KB each.\n\nThe group mixes one real hang (B14.5) with three minor state-hygiene issues. The fixes are independent.",
