        "lenses": [
          {
            "lens": "reproduce",
            "entry": {
              "group_id": "R18",
              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "Both members reproduce on real headless Chromium (chromium 141) on Python 3.13.16 and 3.11.17. Connection._prepare_expert and Connection._prepare_headless (zendriver/core/connection.py) check their done flag, await one or two _send_oneshot calls, and only then set the flag. Nothing serialises this and nothing checks whether the session is still the same one. (1) When two first sends run at the same time (asyncio.gather, or Tab.set_local_storage with 2 items), Page.addScriptToEvaluateOnNewDocument is registered twice. After the next load, element.attachShadow() throws 'RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded'. (2) A detach (tab.aclose()) while the first send is inside the prepare step leaves _prep_headless_done=True, or _prep_expert_done=True, on the detached connection. The next send reattaches a new session but skips the override: navigator.userAgent and the HTTP User-Agent header contain 'HeadlessChrome', or the expert attachShadow override is missing. The same send also starts a Listener on the detached connection; that Listener dies with an unobserved ValueError('no websocket connection'). It also leaves a pending Transaction in mapper, and the next detach fails that Transaction with an exception nobody retrieves.",
              "member_verdicts": [
                {
                  "fid": "B14.2",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Own repro (repro_expert.py, real Chromium, expert=True, headless=True, fresh tab from browser.get(url, new_tab=True), page sets its title from try{div.attachShadow({mode:'closed'})}). Sequential first sends: addScript sent=1, title 'OK'. Running asyncio.gather(tab.evaluate('1'), tab.evaluate('2')): addScript sent=2, title 'ERR:RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded'. tab.set_local_storage({'a':'1','b':'2'}): addScript sent=2, same RangeError. The results repeat across runs and match on py3.11 and py3.13. Sub-claim checked too: in headless mode, concurrent first sends send Network.setUserAgentOverride twice (count 2), with no visible harm."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "B14.6",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Own repro (repro_headless.py, real Chromium, headless=True). race=0 control: _prep_headless_done is None after aclose, and the UA after reattach has no 'Headless'. race=1, gather(tab.evaluate('1'), closer) where closer polls until session_id is set and then awaits tab.aclose(): the first send raises ProtocolException('target session was detached'), and after the detach _prep_headless_done=True. navigator.userAgent and the HTTP User-Agent header after reattach both contain 'HeadlessChrome/141.0.0.0'. Listener.__init__ was called once on a connection with websocket=None and _inbox=None, from Connection.send's 'if not self.listener or not self.listener.running' line, giving 'Task exception was never retrieved | ValueError(no websocket connection)'. A pending Runtime.evaluate tx stays in tab.mapper even after reattach. The next aclose fails it and causes 'Transaction exception was never retrieved | ProtocolException(target session was detached)' (repro_extras.py). The _prepare_expert variant also reproduces (repro_expert_detach.py, expert=True): a detach while the Page.enable oneshot is pending gives _prep_expert_done=True, and after reattach a closed shadow root stays closed ('CLOSED(expert not applied)'; control gives 'OPEN')."
                }
              ],
              "evidence": "Commands (cwd /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/R18-reproduce, PATH has the scratchpad bin with chromium):\n1) timeout 120 /home/user/zendriver/.venv/bin/python repro_expert.py ->\n  zendriver from /home/user/zendriver/zendriver/__init__.py python 3.13.16\n  mode=seq           addScript sent=1 title='OK'\n  mode=gather        addScript sent=2 title='ERR:RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded'\n  mode=localstorage  addScript sent=2 title='ERR:RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded'\n  (the seq and gather rows repeat with the same results; the same output on python 3.11.17 with a scratch package copy, using PYTHONPATH=pkg and a 3.11 venv)\n2) timeout 120 .venv/bin/python repro_headless.py 0 / 1 ->\n  race=0: _prep_headless_done = None; UA 'Mozilla/5.0 ... Chrome/141.0.0.0 Safari/537.36'; zombies 0; loop errors 0\n  race=1: first send result ProtocolException('target session was detached'); after detach _prep_headless_done = True, mapper = {1: Runtime.evaluate pending}; navigator.userAgent after reattach '... HeadlessChrome/141.0.0.0 ...'; 'HTTP header after reattach: UA-HEADER:... HeadlessChrome/141.0.0.0 ...'; zombie Listener() calls 1 (stack: tab.py evaluate -> connection.py line 643 in send: self.listener = Listener(self)); 'Task exception was never retrieved | ValueError('no websocket connection')'. The same on py3.11.\n3) repro_expert_detach.py 0 / 1 -> race=0 'OPEN(expert applied)'; race=1 first send ValueError('no websocket connection'), _prep_expert_done = True, title 'CLOSED(expert not applied)'.\n4) repro_extras.py -> setUserAgentOverride sent: 2 under gather; orphan Runtime.evaluate is still in mapper after reattach; loop errors 'Transaction exception was never retrieved | ProtocolException('target session was detached')' and 'Task exception was never retrieved | ValueError('no websocket connection')'.\nCode read: in Connection.send, expert prepare runs before headless prepare, then comes the 'listener not running -> Listener(self)' check, then the tx goes into mapper before the 'websocket is None -> raise' check. _prepare_headless and _prepare_expert set their flags with setattr after their awaits. _send_oneshot swallows ProtocolException but raises ValueError when websocket is None. _detach_session pops both flags and fails the pending txs.",
              "refinements": "1) In expert mode the detach race has a second symptom. If the detach lands during the addScript oneshot, the next _send_oneshot (Page.enable, or the headless UA one) raises ValueError('no websocket connection') out of send(), not a ProtocolException, and the flag stays unset. If the detach lands during Page.enable, _prep_expert_done is set on the detached connection and the expert override is missing after reattach. So the leak depends on which await the detach interrupts. 2) The orphan tx does not show up as 'never retrieved' right away. It stays pending in mapper, even across reattach, until the next _detach_session fails it. 3) The gather race does not depend on the Python version: it reproduced the same way on 3.11.17 and 3.13.16. 4) Realism: B14.2 is triggered by normal public API use (set_local_storage with 2 or more items, or any concurrent first calls on a new tab in expert mode). B14.6 needs a detach while the first send is in flight (a concurrent tab.aclose(), 'async with tab', or Target.detachedFromTarget/stop), which is rarer. A fix should serialise preparation per session, for example with an in-progress future or lock, and should not set the flag, or should re-check the session, when the session changed during the awaits. Ideally send() should also not start a Listener, or register a tx, on a connection whose websocket is None.",
              "chrome_claims": [
