        },
        "lenses": [
          {
            "lens": "reproduce",
            "entry": {
              "group_id": "R19",
              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "Confirmed by running it. Listener.listener_loop (connection.py, the callback dispatch around line 999-1002) runs every non-coroutine-function handler through asyncio.create_task(asyncio.to_thread(callback, *args)), so it executes in a worker thread with no event loop. (a) Connection.feed_cdp (line 543-556) calls asyncio.ensure_future(self.send(cdp_obj)), which raises RuntimeError \"There is no current event loop in thread 'asyncio_N'\" in that thread. Fetch.continueRequest is never sent. The only trace is 'Task exception was never retrieved' plus 'coroutine Connection.send was never awaited'. With real headless Chromium, Page.navigate hangs until the request is continued by hand from the loop thread. The same code with an async handler works. (b) A lambda that returns a coroutine, a lambda that calls asyncio.create_task, and an object with an async __call__ all fail inspect.iscoroutinefunction. They are run in the thread, and the returned coroutine is dropped ('never awaited'); the create_task case raises 'no running event loop'. The async work never runs. Reproduced on Python 3.13.16 and on 3.11.17, both with websockets 14.1.",
              "member_verdicts": [
                {
                  "fid": "A2.6",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "(a) fake peer and real Chromium: a sync def handler calling tab.feed_cdp runs in thread asyncio_0, RuntimeError 'There is no current event loop', continueRequest never sent, navigate hangs. (b) lambda e: process(e) -> 'coroutine ... process was never awaited', work ran 0 times. lambda e: asyncio.create_task(...) -> RuntimeError('no running event loop'), work ran 0. Object with async __call__ -> iscoroutinefunction False, never awaited, work ran 0. All reproduced on py3.13 (lambda-coro also on py3.11)."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "B14.4",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "The exact form, lambda ev, t: t.feed_cdp(cdp.fetch.continue_request(...)), with real Chromium: the handler ran in thread asyncio_1 and the loop error was RuntimeError(\"There is no current event loop in thread 'asyncio_1'.\"). page.navigate HUNG for more than 8s, and the stuck stack is Connection.send -> 'return await tx' (connection.py:662) waiting on the Page.navigate Transaction. A manual continue_request from the loop thread completed it. Reproduced on 3.11 and 3.13 (3.12 shows the same mechanism in a stdlib-only check). Not reproduced: the side claim that asyncio.Event.set from a handler thread is unsafe. In my run it woke the waiter in under 1 ms, with or without debug mode."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "A12.3",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Same root cause and same reproduction. A sync handler with signature (ev, conn) calling conn.feed_cdp raises RuntimeError from ensure_future inside feed_cdp. The request stays paused and navigation does not complete. The error appears only as an unretrieved-task log. I used Page.navigate with an 8s wait rather than tab.get(timeout=5)."
                }
              ],
              "evidence": "Scratch dir: /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/R19-reproduce/\n\n1) Fake CDP peer. The peer answers every command and emits Fetch.requestPaused after Fetch.enable (or Runtime.consoleAPICalled after Runtime.enable). It records whether Fetch.continueRequest arrives.\nCommand: cd <scratch> && timeout 120 /home/user/zendriver/.venv/bin/python -W always fake_peer.py\nOutput (py3.13.16, zendriver from /home/user/zendriver/zendriver/__init__.py):\n  kind=async: Fetch.continueRequest RECEIVED by peer; handler thread=['MainThread']\n  feed_cdp raised inside handler: RuntimeError There is no current event loop in thread 'asyncio_0'.\n  RuntimeWarning: coroutine 'Connection.send' was never awaited\n  kind=sync: Fetch.continueRequest NEVER sent within 3s (request stays paused); handler thread=['asyncio_0','asyncio_0']\n  loop error: RuntimeError(\"There is no current event loop in thread 'asyncio_0'.\") | Task exception was never retrieved\n  kind=sync-conn (lambda ev, c: c.feed_cdp(...)): NEVER sent within 3s\n  kind=lambda-coro: inspect.iscoroutinefunction(cb)=False; RuntimeWarning: coroutine 'run.<locals>.process' was never awaited; async work ran 0 time(s) (expected 1)\n  kind=lambda-task: async work ran 0; loop error: RuntimeError('no running event loop') | Task exception was never retrieved\n  kind=async-call-obj: iscoroutinefunction=False; coroutine 'H.__call__' was never awaited; async work ran 0\nThe same script on py3.11.17, run from a scratch copy in a throwaway venv (zendriver __file__ printed as the scratch pkg), gave the same sync and lambda-coro results.\n\n2) Real headless Chromium plus a local http.server.\nCommand: PATH=<scratchpad>/bin:$PATH timeout 120 /home/user/zendriver/.venv/bin/python real_chrome.py\n  kind=async: navigate returned FrameId(...); title='OK'; handler calls=[('MainThread', 'http://127.0.0.1:35173/page')]\n  kind=sync: page.navigate HUNG > 8s; handler calls=[('asyncio_0', ...)]\n    stuck task stack: Task coro=<Connection.send() running at zendriver/core/connection.py:662> wait_for=<Transaction method: Page.navigate status: pending> ... line 662, in send: return await tx\n    after manual Fetch.continueRequest(interception-job-2.0) from loop thread: navigate done=True\n    loop error: RuntimeError(\"There is no current event loop in thread 'asyncio_0'.\") | Task exception was never retrieved\n  kind=lambda-conn: same hang in thread asyncio_1, also released by a manual continue.\nThe browser was stopped with await browser.stop() in a finally block.\n\n3) mech.py: stdlib only, asyncio.ensure_future called inside asyncio.to_thread. It raises 'There is no current event loop in thread asyncio_0' on 3.11.17, 3.12.3 and 3.13.16.\n\nCode read fresh:\n- Listener.listener_loop: 'if inspect.iscoroutinefunction(callback): asyncio.create_task(callback(*args)) else: asyncio.create_task(asyncio.to_thread(callback, *args))'. The to_thread task is never observed.\n- Connection.feed_cdp: its docstring says 'used ... during cdp.fetch.RequestPaused events ... note: this is not an async method, just a regular method!', and its body is asyncio.ensure_future(self.send(cdp_obj)).\n- add_handler docstring: 'handlers can be regular callback functions or async coroutine functions (and also just lamba's)'.",
              "refinements": "- The shipped example (examples/fetch_domain.py) uses an async handler, which works. The bug appears only with sync defs, lambdas and async-__call__ objects. Those are documented as valid handlers (add_handler docstring), and feed_cdp's docstring stresses that it is a plain method.\n- A side effect, not part of this group: when a RequestPaused handler is registered, aopen() -> _register_handlers auto-sends Fetch.enable (id 1) before the explicit cdp.fetch.enable() (id 2). The peer saw Fetch.enable twice, so two requestPaused events (one per enable) reached the handler.\n- The B14.4 side claim about asyncio.Event.set from a sync handler was not reproduced: the waiter woke in under 1 ms, with and without debug mode. Only loop-bound calls that need a current or running loop (ensure_future, create_task, get_event_loop) fail outright.\n- On 3.12+, _ensure_future may close the coroutine. The 'never awaited' warning still appeared on 3.13 in my run, but do not rely on that warning as the test oracle. Assert that the peer received Fetch.continueRequest.\n- A fix only in feed_cdp (capture the loop and use call_soon_threadsafe / run_coroutine_threadsafe when off-loop) fixes (a) but not (b). Fixing (b) also needs the dispatch to await an awaitable returned by a sync callable, or to detect async __call__.",
              "chrome_claims": [
                {
                  "claim": "With real headless Chromium, a sync RequestPaused handler calling tab.feed_cdp(continue_request) leaves the request paused and Page.navigate hangs, while the async-handler control completes with title 'OK'",
                  "status": "verified",
                  "how": "real_chrome.py run against Chromium headless and a local http.server: 'page.navigate HUNG > 8s', the stuck stack is at Connection.send line 662, and a manual continue_request from the loop thread released it"
                },
                {
                  "claim": "The lambda (ev, t) form receives the Tab as its second argument and hangs the same way",
                  "status": "verified",
                  "how": "real_chrome.py kind=lambda-conn: handler ran in thread asyncio_1, navigate hung"
                }
              ],
              "realism": "medium",
              "severity": "hang",
              "fix_assessment": {
                "kind": "minimal-local",
