            "lens": "fixsafety",
            "entry": {
              "group_id": "R20",
              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "Confirmed on real headless Chromium 141. When `Element.send_keys` gets a str, it calls `KeyEvents.from_text(text, KeyPressEvent.CHAR)`. That maps a lone '\\n' or '\\r' grapheme to `SpecialKeys.ENTER`. `_get_key_and_text` (CHAR branch) then calls `conv_to_str(ENTER)` (zendriver/core/keys.py, `KeyEvents.conv_to_str`, around line 167), which returns '\\n'. Chrome turns `Input.dispatchKeyEvent(type='char', text='\\n')` into keypress charCode 10. That inserts nothing and does not trigger implicit form submission. Only '\\r' (charCode 13) acts as Enter, which is the value the class's own `SPECIAL_KEY_CHAR_MAP` and the DOWN_AND_UP path already use. Changing that one line to `return \"\\r\"` fixes it.",
              "member_verdicts": [
                {
                  "fid": "A10.4",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Reproduced with my own probe on Chromium 141.0.7390.37, headless, Python 3.13, repo code. textarea.send_keys('line1\\nline2\\rline3\\r\\nline4') gives 'line1line2line3\\nline4'. input.send_keys('abc\\n') and input.send_keys('abc\\r') both give submits=0 and keypress charCode 10. Raw char '\\r' inserts a newline and submits=1. contenteditable send_keys('a\\nb') gives 'ab'. CRLF already works because '\\r\\n' is a single grapheme and is sent as raw char text '\\r\\n' (charCode 13). With the prototype fix the results are 'line1\\nline2\\nline3\\nline4', submits=1 for 'abc\\n' and 'abc\\r', and contenteditable 'a<div>b</div>'."
                }
              ],
              "evidence": "Probe: /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/R20-fixsafety/probe/probe.py, run against page.html in the same folder. Repo run (zendriver from /home/user/zendriver/zendriver/__init__.py): \"send_keys textarea 'line1\\nline2\\rline3\\r\\nline4' -> ta:'line1line2line3\\nline4'\", \"send_keys input 'abc\\n' -> submits:0, kp charCode 10\", \"raw char '\\r' input -> submits:1\". Prototype run (zendriver from .../R20-fixsafety/pkg/zendriver/__init__.py): \"ta:'line1\\nline2\\nline3\\nline4'\", \"send_keys input 'abc\\n' -> submits:1, charCode 13\".\n\nRegression test /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/R20-fixsafety/tests/test_r20_newline.py has 3 browser-free payload tests and 1 real-Chromium textarea/form test.\n- Repo (zendriver imported from /home/user/zendriver/zendriver/__init__.py): '4 failed, 1 passed in 0.93s'. Failures include \"assert ['a', '\\n', 'b', '\\n', 'c'] == ['a', '\\r', 'b', '\\r', 'c']\" and \"assert 'line1line2line3' == 'line1\\nline2\\nline3'\".\n- Prototype (PYTHONPATH=.../R20-fixsafety/pkg, zendriver imported from the pkg copy): '5 passed in 1.32s'.\n\nThe existing repo tests tests/core/test_keyinputs.py and tests/core/test_react_controlled_input.py, run from a scratch copy against the prototype, headless: '5 passed in 3.55s'.",
              "refinements": "1. CRLF ('\\r\\n') is not affected: it is one grapheme and goes out as raw char text, so the bug only hits a lone '\\n' or a lone '\\r'.\n2. The minimal fix covers native line insertion (textarea, contenteditable) and native implicit form submission. It does not cover JS handlers listening on keydown: CHAR mode fires only keypress. With the fix, send_keys('q\\n') still logs only [\"keypress:\",\"keypress:\"], with e.key == '' and no keydown/keyup. SPAs that handle Enter in onKeyDown still will not react. Fixing that is a design change, for example emitting DOWN_AND_UP for ENTER inside from_text even in CHAR mode. It is not needed for this group.\n3. `KeyEvents(SpecialKeys.ENTER).to_cdp_events(KeyPressEvent.CHAR)` is public API. Its payload text changes from '\\n' to '\\r', which is an improvement.",
