                "risks": "- Pure synchronous mapping change: no locks, no re-entrancy, no cancel or error paths touched.\n- Behaviour change callers will notice: newlines in str text sent to an <input> inside a form now submit the form at each newline. Before, they were silently dropped. Multi-line text into a textarea or contenteditable now gets real line breaks or paragraphs. This matches the send_keys docstring, which recommends sending \\n, and what a real user's Enter does.\n- Public conv_to_str(ENTER) and to_cdp_events(CHAR) for ENTER now return '\\r'.\n- Keydown-based Enter handlers are still not triggered (pre-existing CHAR-mode limitation, see refinements).\n- mypy: I ran .venv/bin/mypy --config-file pyproject.toml from /home/user/zendriver with a scratch --cache-dir, using the venv binary directly instead of `uv run` so the venv cannot be synced. The untouched copy and the prototype both report the same 332 errors in 47 files. All of them are in generated zendriver/cdp/ code; there are 0 in keys.py and 0 new."
