                }
              ],
              "evidence": "Commands (cwd = scratch dir, PATH includes scratchpad/bin): `timeout 120 /home/user/zendriver/.venv/bin/python p1_restart_after_stop.py` -> 'zendriver from /home/user/zendriver/zendriver/__init__.py', 'after stop: _process None _process_pid None config host/port 127.0.0.1 43373 info stale: True targets kept: 1 connection closed: True', 'restart raised after 2.51s: ConnectionRefusedError(111, \"Connect call failed (\\'127.0.0.1\\', 43373)\")' at browser.py line 637 in start (await self.connection.send(cdp.target.set_discover_targets(...))), 'chrome children: []'. `p2_restart_after_crash.py` -> 'killed; poll() -9 stopped True', 'start after crash raised after 2.51s: Exception: --- Failed to connect to browser ---', 'processes launched by restart: []'. `p3_restart_manual_reset.py` -> 'first tab is stale (old id): True', 'atexit callbacks registered: []', 'get after restart raised ProtocolException No target with given id found command:Target.attachToTarget'. `p4_hostport_connected.py` -> 'B16.13 stopped property: True | connection closed: False | tabs: 1 | _process: None', 'A3.10 second start(): ... connection replaced: True | old still open: True | old listener running: True', 'established sockets to chrome before 2nd start: 1' -> 'after 2nd start: 2', 'after _atexit_cleanup(): connection closed: False | old closed: False | established sockets: 2', 'after explicit aclose of both: established sockets: 0'. `p5_atexit_loop_close.py` -> 'after loop close: atexit hook called _stop? [] | connection.closed: False'. All scripts are in /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/R23-reproduce/. Every Chrome I started was stopped, and the temp user-data dirs were removed (0 chromium processes left afterwards).",
              "refinements": "Root cause, read from the code: Browser.start (browser.py around lines 530-535) writes the auto-chosen host/port into self.config, and connect_existing is decided only from `config.host is not None and config.port is not None`. So the config cannot tell user-supplied values from auto-chosen ones. Browser._stop (around lines 874-917) clears _process/_process_pid but not config.host/port, self.info, self.targets or self.connection. Extra findings: (1) The dead-process branch `return await self.create(config=self.config)` returns a new Browser instead of restarting self, so `await b.start()` without using the result leaves b dead even once host/port are fixed. The fresh instance is also registered with atexit while the old one stays in registered_instances. (2) update_targets never prunes the stale targets from the first run, so after a manual host/port reset tabs[0]/main_tab are dead Tab objects. (3) For B16.13, changing `stopped` so the atexit hook runs _stop() for connect-existing browsers would send Browser.close to a Chrome the user launched, which is a behaviour change. A fix should base `stopped` on the connection, and close only the websocket/forwarders at exit, not the remote browser. (4) The start() guard `if self._process or self._process_pid` does not cover connect-existing, so start() is not idempotent there (A3.10). Fix candidates: reset auto-chosen host/port in _stop (or keep a private flag for user-provided values), clear info/targets/connection on stop, and guard start() on `self.connection and not self.connection.closed`.",
