                  "status": "verified",
                  "how": "p5_kill_stop.py (repo stop and prototype start) and p6_retry.py (prototype fails on the first attempt and succeeds on retry; succeeds on the first attempt with a Q3-style aclose catch)"
                }
              ],
              "realism": "high",
              "severity": "crash",
              "fix_assessment": {
                "kind": "minimal-local",
                "prototype_dir": "/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/R23-fixsafety/pkg",
                "diff_summary": "Only zendriver/core/browser.py; the full diff is in /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/R23-fixsafety/fix.diff. (a) stopped: `if self._process: return self._process.poll() is not None`, else `return not self.connection or self.connection.closed`. (b) _atexit_cleanup: `if self._process and not self.stopped: await self._stop()`, so atexit behaviour is unchanged and an external browser is still left running. (c) start(): the crash branch becomes `if self._process and self._process.poll() is not None: await self._stop()` (restart in place, returns self), then `if self._process: warn and return self`. (d) start(): after util.get_registered_instances().add(self), unregister and register self._atexit_cleanup (moved from create(), which no longer registers), and set self.info = None before the test_connection loop. (e) start(): `if self.connection: await self.connection.aclose()` before `self.connection = Connection(...)`. (f) _stop(): inside the `if self._process:` block, set config.host/port to None (start() always chose them for a browser it launched); at the end, before _cleanup_temporary_profile, call self.targets.clear().",
                "regression_test_path": "/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/R23-fixsafety/tests/test_r23_restart.py",
                "fails_on_repo": "yes",
                "passes_on_prototype": "yes",
                "mypy_ok": "yes",
                "risks": "Behaviour changes callers would notice: start() on a dead browser now restarts the same Browser and returns self instead of a new instance (the old path always failed). After stop(), browser.tabs is [] and config.host/port are None for launched browsers. websocket_url still returns the old URL until the next start(). A second start() on a live host/port browser now reconnects and closes the old connection: in-flight tab commands fail with 'target session was detached', and Tab objects reattach lazily through the new connection (checked on real Chromium: the old tab's evaluate still worked). atexit registration moved from create() into start(), so a subclass that overrides start() without calling super() loses it. A browser whose start() raised after launching is now killed when the loop closes instead of leaking. Residual risks: start() right after a crash can raise until Q3's aclose fix lands (a retry works). Two concurrent start() calls on a crashed browser launch two Chromes, and the racing _stop terminates one, leaving one live Chrome (probe p7). The repo had no crash path that worked, and concurrent start() after a normal stop is still serialised because nothing awaits before _start_process. For host/port browsers whose remote died, `stopped` stays False because Connection.closed only becomes True on aclose. No locks were added, so there are no re-entrancy or lock-ordering problems. mypy shows no new errors (all 332 are in cdp/, the same on the untouched copy; 0 in core). ruff check and ruff format pass. The full non-external suite passes 104 tests with 1 skipped, the same as the untouched copy."
