        "lenses": [
          {
            "lens": "reproduce",
            "entry": {
              "group_id": "R24",
              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "Reproduced against a real headless Chromium (141.0.7390.37) on Python 3.13.16. I started Chromium myself by absolute path with --remote-debugging-port, so there was a live DevTools endpoint, and ran with PATH=/usr/bin:/bin, which has no chrome, chromium, brave or msedge binary on it. Under those conditions zendriver.start(host, port), Browser.create(host=, port=), create_from_undetected_chromedriver(driver) and a bare Config(host=, port=) all raise FileNotFoundError('could not find a valid browser binary...'). The error comes from Config.__init__ (config.py line 89-90, `if not browser_executable_path: browser_executable_path = find_executable(browser)`), before any connection attempt. Two controls show the binary is never used on this path. Passing browser_executable_path='/does/not/exist' against the same endpoint connects (Chrome/141.0.7390.37, 1 tab, b._process is None). The same calls with chromium on PATH also connect. Browser.start only checks the executable inside `if not connect_existing:`, so in host+port mode the autodetection in Config.__init__ only gets in the way.",
              "member_verdicts": [
                {
                  "fid": "A3.9",
