                "risks": "Deferring the lookup when host and port are set (or making it lazy) leaves browser_executable_path as None. Browser.start only reads it under `not connect_existing`, but it also feeds a logger.info of `exe`, and tests/core/test_drm.py does str(browser.config.browser_executable_path), so code paths that format it must tolerate None. create_from_undetected_chromedriver sets conf.host and conf.port after Config(), so a lookup that only checks __init__ arguments would not cover it unless that function passes host and port to the constructor or the lookup becomes lazy."
              }
