              "group_id": "R24",
              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "Config.__init__ (zendriver/core/config.py, the `if not browser_executable_path: browser_executable_path = find_executable(browser)` block) looks up a local browser binary on every call. When no Chrome, Brave or Edge is installed, connecting to an existing or remote browser fails with FileNotFoundError before any connection is attempted, although Browser.start never uses the executable when connect_existing is true. This was reproduced with real Chromium (launched by absolute path, PATH without any chrome) through zd.start(host, port), Browser.create(host, port) and util.create_from_undetected_chromedriver. create_from_undetected_chromedriver calls Config() with no host or port and sets them afterwards, so skipping the lookup only in Config.__init__ does not fix it: util.py has to pass host and port into Config(...). A minimal local fix was prototyped and checked.",
