              "evidence": "Python 3.13.16. Real Chromium repro (/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/R24-fixsafety/repro_real.py, default PATH, no chrome): repo copy (zendriver from /home/user/zendriver/zendriver/__init__.py) gives 'zd.start(host,port) -> raised FileNotFoundError could not find a valid browser binary...', the same for Browser.create(host,port) and create_from_undetected_chromedriver. The prototype (zendriver from .../R24-fixsafety/pkg/zendriver/__init__.py) gives 'connected OK: Chrome/141.0.7390.37' for all three. Browser-free regression test /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/R24-fixsafety/tests/test_r24_remote_no_local_browser.py uses find_executable patched to raise, plus a fake DevTools peer: websockets serve with process_request answering /json/version, and CDP replies for Target.setDiscoverTargets, Target.getTargets and Browser.close. Repo run: 'zendriver imported from /home/user/zendriver/zendriver/__init__.py ... 4 failed, 1 passed, 1 skipped'. Prototype run (PYTHONPATH=pkg): 'zendriver imported from .../R24-fixsafety/pkg/zendriver/__init__.py ... 6 passed in 0.42s'.",
              "refinements": "The triage strategy ('defer lookup when host and port are given') is not enough alone. util.create_from_undetected_chromedriver builds Config() with no host or port and assigns conf.host/conf.port afterwards, so it must pass Config(host=host, port=int(port)) instead. Browser.start also reads self.config.browser_executable_path outside the connect_existing guard (`exe = ...` before params). That is harmless at runtime once the value is None, but mypy needs narrowing before util._start_process(exe, ...). Using the same `host is None or port is None` test as Browser.start's connect_existing keeps the two in step.",
