                "prototype_dir": "/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/R24-fixsafety/pkg",
                "diff_summary": "config.py Config.__init__: `if not browser_executable_path and (host is None or port is None): browser_executable_path = find_executable(browser)`, with a comment that connecting to an existing browser starts no local browser. util.py create_from_undetected_chromedriver: parse debugger_address first, then `conf = Config(host=host, port=int(port))`, dropping the later conf.host/conf.port assignment. browser.py Browser.start: hoist `exe = self.config.browser_executable_path` above the `if not connect_existing:` check, change the check to `if not exe or not pathlib.Path(exe).exists(): raise FileNotFoundError(...)` (the existing message), and add `assert exe is not None  # checked above` before util._start_process for mypy (same style as proxy.py). Alternative variant in .../R24-fixsafety/pkg2: keep the lookup but swallow FileNotFoundError only when host and port are both given. This keeps browser_executable_path filled in and the browser-name ValueError check whenever a local browser exists. It passes the same 6 tests and is mypy-clean.",
                "regression_test_path": "/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/R24-fixsafety/tests/test_r24_remote_no_local_browser.py",
                "fails_on_repo": "yes",
                "passes_on_prototype": "yes",
                "mypy_ok": "yes",
                "risks": "No locks, re-entrancy or cancel paths are touched. Changes callers would notice: (1) Config(host=..., port=...).browser_executable_path is now None instead of the autodetected path, and its inferred type widens from `str | Path` to `str | Path | None`, so a downstream strict-mypy user doing Path(config.browser_executable_path) gets a new error. (2) An invalid `browser=` value is no longer rejected (ValueError) when host and port are given. (3) Rare case: a Config built with host+port and later switched to a local launch (host/port reset to None) used to launch the autodetected binary. It now fails with the clear 'Could not determine browser executable' FileNotFoundError (thanks to the `not exe` guard), not a TypeError from Path(None). The pkg2 'try/except FileNotFoundError only if host and port given' variant avoids (1)-(3) whenever a local browser exists, at the cost of a pointless filesystem scan. mypy: 332 errors, all under zendriver/cdp, for both the untouched copy and the prototype, so no new errors (run with .venv/bin/mypy --config-file pyproject.toml and a scratch --cache-dir to avoid writing into the repo). ruff check and format pass. Unrelated, not fixed: Browser.start still calls self.config() on the connect_existing path, which lazily creates a temp profile dir for a remote browser."
              }
