              "evidence": "Test /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/BA-fixsafety/R17/test_r17.py, real Chromium plus a local http.server. Download behaviour is set to deny so no files are written. On the repo, which printed 'zendriver imported from /home/user/zendriver/zendriver/__init__.py': '3 failed, 1 passed in 12.93s' (test_get_returns_for_204 TimeoutError, test_get_returns_for_download TimeoutError, test_get_new_tab_timeout_does_not_leave_the_tab_open). On the prototype, which printed '.../verify/BA-fixsafety/R17/pkg/zendriver/__init__.py': '4 passed in 4.06s'. The repo core suite (headless, not external) on the prototype: '105 passed, 1 skipped, 4 deselected'. ruff format and ruff check are clean.",
              "refinements": "Interaction with R25: with autodiscover_targets=False, every Browser.get(new_tab) times out. With only the R17 prototype applied, it now creates the tab, closes it and raises (verified with probe_cross.py: targets 1 -> 1, TimeoutError). The R25 fix must land with or before the R17 close-on-timeout change. The errorText early return covers only the existing-tab path; new_tab + 204 needs the R35 design. The early return skips 'connection.browser = self', which does no harm for tabs[0].",
