              "group_id": "R25",
              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "Confirmed on real headless Chromium with config.autodiscover_targets=False. Browser.get(url) and Browser.get(new_tab=True) always raise TimeoutError although the navigation succeeded. Tab.close() closes the tab, then waits 10 s and raises TimeoutError. update_targets never drops destroyed targets, so main_tab and tabs[0] stay on the closed tab and browser.get then fails with 'No target with given id found'. A small prototype fixes all four. It always sends Target.setDiscoverTargets(discover=True) but installs the _handle_target_update tracking handlers only when autodiscover_targets is set. update_targets prunes targets that getTargets no longer lists. The TargetInfoChanged/TargetDestroyed lookups in _handle_target_update tolerate a target that is already missing.",
