              "summary": "Confirmed on real headless Chromium 141. The headless UA override and the expert attachShadow patch are applied lazily, inside a Tab's first Connection.send. So the first document of a tab opened with Browser.get(new_tab=True), Browser.create_context(url), or window.open popups is requested with 'HeadlessChrome' in User-Agent, and page JS sees navigator.userAgent containing 'Headless'. The expert patch is also missing on that first document. The main tab is unaffected because Browser.get sends Page.navigate through the tab, which runs the preparation first. A reload of the new tab is clean.",
              "member_verdicts": [
                {
                  "fid": "A2.5",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Server log (path, UA has HeadlessChrome, Sec-Fetch-Dest): /main-tab False; /new-tab True, and its JS beacon reported navigator.userAgent includes Headless = true; /ctx (create_context) True; /popup-open (window.open from the main tab) True; /new-tab after reload False. Expert mode: attachShadow({mode:'closed'}) yielded an open shadow root on /main-tab (open=true), not on the first /new-tab load (open=false), and did after reload (open=true). Sec-CH-UA had no 'Headless' in any case."
                }
