              "evidence": "r35_probe.py and r35_expert.py in /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/BA-refute/. Code: Connection.send calls _prepare_expert/_prepare_headless only on the connection doing the send. Browser.get(new_tab) sends Target.createTarget(url) on the browser connection and then only waits for events, so the new Tab never sends before its first document loads. create_context does the same with createTarget(url, browser_context_id). The lazy design comes unchanged from upstream (5c1a005); 984bf02 only added client-hint metadata. test_headless_user_agent covers only browser.get on the main tab.",
              "refinements": "Only affects headless=True (and expert=True for the shadow patch). It hits the first document, and its subresources and scripts, of tabs created with a URL by Chrome or zendriver without a prior send on the Tab: new_tab/new_window, create_context(url), and popups or target=_blank. Workaround: open the new tab at about:blank and then call tab.get(url). Passing Config(user_agent=...) sets --user-agent globally, which should also hide the token (assumed, not run). new_tab=True appears in docs/quickstart.md, so stealth users in headless mode can plausibly hit this.",
