          {
            "lens": "fixsafety",
            "entry": {
              "group_id": "R35",
              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "Confirmed on real headless Chromium: the first document request of Browser.get(new_tab=True) and of Browser.create_context(url) carries 'HeadlessChrome' in its User-Agent, and page JS during load on the new tab sees it too. Later requests and reloads do not. Popups opened with window.open() and target=_blank links also load with HeadlessChrome, and the minimal fix cannot touch those. The minimal fix (create the target at about:blank, then navigate through the tab's own session so _prepare_headless runs first) fixes the UA for get(new_tab) and create_context. It has two side effects: the new tab's history.length goes from 1 to 2, and the slow first navigation is no longer covered by the get() timeout. So the right fix is a design change (browser-level auto-attach with waitForDebuggerOnStart).",
              "member_verdicts": [
                {
                  "fid": "A2.5",
