                "kind": "design-api",
                "prototype_dir": "/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/BA-fixsafety/R35/pkg",
                "diff_summary": "Minimal attempt (diff saved in .../R35/browser.diff). Browser.get(new_tab) creates the target at 'about:blank' and then always does `await connection.send(cdp.page.navigate(url))` (the first send runs _prepare_headless/_prepare_expert before navigating). create_context creates at about:blank, then `tab_ = await self._get_tab(target_id); await tab_.send(cdp.page.navigate(url))`. Recommended design instead: in Browser.start, send Target.setAutoAttach(auto_attach=True, wait_for_debugger_on_start=True, flatten=True) on the browser connection. Handle Target.attachedToTarget by binding the session to the Tab (set session_id instead of a second attachToTarget in _attach_session), applying the UA override and expert script, then Runtime.runIfWaitingForDebugger. This covers createTarget, contexts and popups with no extra history entry and no timeout change.",
                "regression_test_path": "/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/BA-fixsafety/R35/test_r35.py",
                "fails_on_repo": "yes",
                "passes_on_prototype": "no",
                "mypy_ok": "yes",
                "risks": "Risks of the minimal fix: (a) the new tab's history.length goes from 1 to 2, so tab.back() now returns to about:blank, and the fingerprint changes; (b) the first navigation now sits in Page.navigate, which waits for the response and is outside the get() timeout, so get(new_tab, timeout) can block for the server's full latency (verified 3 s vs 0.5 s); it must be combined with the get-timeout PR putting navigate under the timeout; (c) popups are not fixed. Risks of the auto-attach design: every new target pauses until zendriver resumes it, so a failing or slow attach handler would hang page loads and popups. The Runtime.evaluate fallback in _prepare_headless (used when no headless UA metadata exists) may not answer on a paused target. The handler must run in its own task and never block the listener. It also overlaps with the lazy _attach_session (_attach_lock) and needs care to avoid double attach."
              }
            }
          }
        ]
