            "lens": "fixsafety",
            "entry": {
              "group_id": "R41",
              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "All five members confirmed. Browser iteration crashes with no page tabs, with only non-page targets, in nested loops and after exhaustion; zip() pairs the wrong tabs; reversed() is not an iterator. grant_all_permissions always fails on Chromium 141 Linux. tile_windows lays windows out over about a third of the screen, divides by zero with no windows, and never closes mss. CookieJar.save/load match the pattern against str(cookie.__dict__). Local fixes pass a browser-free test (plus one real-Chromium test for permissions) that fails on the repo. One fix-safety trap: the obvious per-type grant loop is wrong, because every Browser.grantPermissions call denies all types it does not list.",
              "member_verdicts": [
                {
                  "fid": "A4.1",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Browser-free: list(empty) raised AttributeError '_i'. Only a service_worker target: ValueError 'not in list'. The nested comprehension raised AttributeError, and so did next(it) after exhaustion. next(reversed(b)) raised TypeError 'list' object is not an iterator. The (c) zip mis-pairing follows from the same shared cursor. Fix: __iter__ returns iter(self.tabs) and __reversed__ returns reversed(self.tabs); __next__ and _i are removed. main_tab is always tabs[0] when any page exists (stable sort), so iteration order is unchanged."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "A4.6",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Real Chromium 141: 'ProtocolException Unknown permission type: localNetwork'. Granting one type at a time rejected handTracking, protectedMediaIdentifier, smartCard and webPrinting (\"can't be granted in current context\") and localNetwork and loopbackNetwork (unknown); 33 types were accepted. The calls are destructive: after the one-at-a-time loop, geolocation, notifications and midi all read 'denied', because each call 'grants the given permissions and rejects all others'. So the fix probes each type, then sends ONE grantPermissions with the accepted set. That leaves geolocation 'granted' on an http origin."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "A4.7",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Fake mss with a 1920x1080 monitor: 1 window gives [[0,0,639,1080]], 2 windows 319 px each, 4 windows 159 px each, all in one row covering about 1/3 of the width. The prototype uses req_cols = max_columns or ceil(sqrt(n)), which fills the full width (2 windows: 959 px each; 4 windows: a 2x2 grid). The formula comes unchanged from upstream nodriver, so maintainers may see it as a layout choice. Cosmetic."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "A4.8",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "(a) tile_windows() with no tabs raised ZeroDivisionError at req_rows = int(num_windows / req_cols). (b) None of the fake mss instances was closed after 3 calls. In site-packages mss 10.0.0, linux.MSS.__init__ calls XOpenDisplay and only close()/__exit__ calls XCloseDisplay, and there is no __del__. Prototype: `with mss.mss() as m:` and an early `return []` when there are no windows."
