              "evidence": "Test /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/BA-fixsafety/R41/test_r41.py: 16 browser-free tests plus 1 real-Chromium test. Repo (printed /home/user/zendriver/zendriver/__init__.py): '17 failed, 1 warning in 1.39s'. Prototype (printed .../R41/pkg/zendriver/__init__.py): '17 passed in 1.09s'. The first per-type-only grant prototype FAILED the real-Chromium test ('AssertionError: denied'), which is how the reject-all-others behaviour was found. probe_perm.py shows 'after single: geolocation denied' and 'after origin grant: granted'. The repo core suite on the prototype gave '105 passed, 1 skipped, 4 deselected'. mypy shows no new errors; ruff is clean.",
              "refinements": "A4.6: the safe fix needs a final combined grant (N+1 calls), not just per-type try/except. The prototype re-raises ProtocolExceptions without a code (connection closed) instead of swallowing them for every type. A4.1(c): besides the crash, the live shared cursor also skips tabs when a loop body closes tabs; the snapshot iterator fixes that too.",
              "chrome_claims": [
                {
                  "claim": "Browser.grantPermissions rejects the whole call when one type is unknown or cannot be granted without an origin (Chromium 141 Linux)",
                  "status": "verified",
                  "how": "probe_perm.py granting each PermissionType on its own"
                },
                {
                  "claim": "Each Browser.grantPermissions call denies every type it does not list",
                  "status": "verified",
                  "how": "after one-at-a-time grants, navigator.permissions.query reported geolocation, notifications and midi as 'denied' instead of 'prompt'"
                }
