              "summary": "Both members reproduced on real headless Chromium 141 with Python 3.13.16. (1) If a RequestPaused handler exists, a manual Fetch.disable is undone on the next send: _register_handlers re-sends Fetch.enable with {} params, every request gets paused, and Page.navigate never returns. The same thing happens after a tab.intercept() block exits while the user has their own RequestPaused handler. (2) After remove_handlers(cdp.fetch.RequestPaused, h), Fetch is dropped from enabled_domains but Fetch.disable is never sent. The browser keeps pausing every request, so tab.get() raises TimeoutError and evaluate() hangs. An explicit Fetch.disable fixes it immediately.",
