              "summary": "I could not refute either member. Both hangs reproduce on real headless Chromium (Python 3.13.16). (1) Connection._register_handlers drops an auto-enabled domain from enabled_domains in its final `for ed in enabled_domains` loop but never sends X.disable. After a RequestPaused handler is removed, Chrome keeps pausing every request and nothing continues them. (2) Connection.send calls _update_manual_domain('disable') after _register_handlers, which removes the domain from both lists. If a RequestPaused handler is still registered, the next send of any kind (aopen() always runs _register_handlers) sends a param-less Fetch.enable, which intercepts every URL.",
