              "summary": "util.cdp_get_module(Domain.lower()) fails for 23 multi-word CDP domains (WebAuthn, FedCm, DOMStorage, IndexedDB, ServiceWorker, ...). Connection._update_manual_domain therefore swallows ModuleNotFoundError, so a manual X.enable(params) is not tracked. Once a handler for that domain exists, the next send re-sends X.enable() with {} params. Reproduced with a fake CDP peer and on real Chromium. Only WebAuthn (enableUI) and FedCm (disableRejectionDelay) have optional enable params that this can reset. That they actually get reset is inferred from the spec defaults and not observable headless.",
