              "refinements": "The practical wrong-result is limited to WebAuthn.enable(enable_ui=...) and FedCm.enable(disable_rejection_delay=...). For the other unmapped domains, enable takes no params, so the re-send is only redundant. For PerformanceTimeline and BluetoothEmulation the auto-enable call raises TypeError on every send (debug-logged). The opposite also holds: an auto-enabled multi-word domain stays in enabled_domains after a manual X.disable, so it is not re-enabled. The collision risk of a bare import_module of a lowercased name with an unrelated top-level module was not observed for any real CDP domain.",
