              "summary": "The mechanism is real. _update_manual_domain calls util.cdp_get_module(domain_name.lower()), which cannot resolve 15 multi-word domains. A manual WebAuthn.enable(enable_ui=True) / FedCm.enable(disable_rejection_delay=True) is therefore not tracked, and after a handler is added the next send carries a param-less WebAuthn.enable / FedCm.enable. The user-visible harm is narrow and not demonstrated. Only WebAuthn and FedCm have optional enable params. The re-send happens only when the manual enable comes BEFORE add_handler. That enableUI / disableRejectionDelay actually get reset is assumed from the CDP spec, not observed.",
              "member_verdicts": [
