              "summary": "_update_manual_domain calls util.cdp_get_module(domain_name.lower()). For any multi-word CDP domain, getattr(cdp, 'webauthn') fails and importlib.import_module('webauthn') raises ModuleNotFoundError, which is swallowed. So a manual X.enable(params) is never tracked, and once a handler is added the next send emits a param-less X.enable. 23 of the 56 CDP domains are affected, not only the 15 listed.",
              "member_verdicts": [
                {
                  "fid": "A9.5",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "All 23 failing domains: BackgroundService, BluetoothEmulation, CacheStorage, CrashReportContext, DOMDebugger, DOMSnapshot, DOMStorage, DeviceAccess, DeviceOrientation, EventBreakpoints, FedCm, FileSystem, HeadlessExperimental, HeapProfiler, IndexedDB, LayerTree, PerformanceTimeline, ServiceWorker, SmartCardEmulation, SystemInfo, WebAudio, WebAuthn, WebMCP. Fake peer: after web_authn.enable(enable_ui=True), manually_enabled_domains was [], and after add_handler(CredentialAdded) the next send emitted [('WebAuthn.enable', {}), ('Page.reload', {})]. FedCm behaved the same. Real Chromium also showed the extra '{\"method\": \"WebAuthn.enable\", \"params\": {}...' frame, but the virtual authenticator kept working (get_credentials OK). The claimed reset of enableUI/disableRejectionDelay is inferred, not observed. The bug only triggers when the manual enable comes before add_handler; with the handler first, the auto-enable goes out before the user's enable."
                }
              ],
              "evidence": "tests/test_r27.py (parametrised over every CDP domain parsed from the generated modules, plus WebAuthn/FedCm tracking against a fake peer). Repo (/home/user/zendriver/zendriver/__init__.py): '25 failed, 33 passed'. Prototype (.../BB-fixsafety/R27/pkg/zendriver/__init__.py): '58 passed'. Chrome probe probes/probe_r27_chrome.py: on the repo, 'manual domains: []' and the frames sent included the WebAuthn.enable {} frame. On the prototype, manual domains were ['zendriver.cdp.web_authn'] and only WebAuthn.getCredentials was sent.",
              "refinements": "The affected list is larger than claimed (23 domains, including CacheStorage, DOMDebugger, EventBreakpoints, FileSystem, SystemInfo, BackgroundService, CrashReportContext and DeviceOrientation). The manual-disable bookkeeping has the mirror-image bug, found by code reading: a manual WebAuthn.disable of an auto-enabled domain is not removed from enabled_domains, so zendriver thinks the domain is on and never re-enables it. _register_handlers itself resolves these domains correctly, because it passes the full dotted module path, which works through import_module.",
              "chrome_claims": [
                {
                  "claim": "In Chrome, the param-less WebAuthn.enable is actually sent after a handler is added",
                  "status": "verified",
                  "how": "Spied tab websocket.send in a real headless Chromium probe"
