              "group_id": "R30",
              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "All four members reproduced on real headless Chromium 141 with Python 3.13.16. (1) A timed-out wait_for on exp.value cancels the shared response_future. A later await raises CancelledError although the task was not cancelled (cancelling()==0), and the event handler hits InvalidStateError. Intercept behaves the same: continue_request raises CancelledError after a timed-out wait on it.request. (2) expect_request on a self-polling page never resolves until an unrelated tab.send enables Network. (3) If the body fails after the headers (ERR_CONTENT_LENGTH_MISMATCH), response_body hangs on loading_finished_future. (4) If the request is refused before any response, exp.value hangs on response_future while request_future is done. Chrome emitted Network.loadingFailed in both failure cases, and nothing handles it.",
