            "lens": "fixsafety",
            "entry": {
              "group_id": "R30",
              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "All four members reproduce. (1) The expect/intercept properties await the bare stored future, so a timed-out wait_for cancels the shared future and the expectation is dead: later awaits raise CancelledError and the handler's set_result raises InvalidStateError. (2) expect_request/expect_response only add handlers on enter. Network.enable is sent on the next tab.send, so a page-initiated request is never seen while the caller just awaits. (3) Network.loadingFailed is not handled, so response_body hangs when the request fails after headers, and value/response hang when it fails before any response.",
              "member_verdicts": [
                {
                  "fid": "A10.3",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "After wait_for(exp.value, 0.1) times out, exp.response_future is <Future cancelled> with current_task().cancelling() == 0 (3.13). A pure-asyncio check shows the same on 3.11.17 and 3.12.3, and asyncio.shield keeps the future pending. Fake peer test: the second await raised CancelledError at expect.py ResponseExpectation.value 'return await self.response_future'. intercept.py uses the identical '(await self.response_future)' pattern (6 sites); that part was checked only by code reading. DownloadExpectation.value has the same pattern."
