                  "fid": "A10.8",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Duplicate of B13.7's failed-after-headers case. response_body hung for 6s on the repo while Chrome emitted Network.loadingFailed net::ERR_CONTENT_LENGTH_MISMATCH. The prototype raises quickly."
                }
              ],
              "evidence": "tests/test_r30.py (fake peer that only emits Network events after Network.enable). Repo (/home/user/zendriver/zendriver/__init__.py): '4 failed in 6.51s' (CancelledError; TimeoutError x3). Prototype (.../BB-fixsafety/R30/pkg/zendriver/__init__.py): '4 passed in 0.56s', with no loop-handler errors. Chrome probe probes/probe_r30_chrome.py on the repo: 'A10.7 ... still pending after 4s', 'A10.8 expect_response.response_body: still pending after 6s', 'LoadingFailed seen: [net::ERR_CONTENT_LENGTH_MISMATCH]', 'B13.7 refused: expect_response.value: still pending after 5s', 'request_future done: True'. On the prototype: A10.7 resolved; response_body and value raised 'ProtocolException: loading failed: net::ERR_CONTENT_LENGTH_MISMATCH' and '... net::ERR_UNSAFE_PORT'.",
