                "prototype_dir": "/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/BB-fixsafety/R30/pkg",
                "diff_summary": "expect.py: every property await is wrapped in asyncio.shield (request, response, response_body for both futures, RequestExpectation.value, ResponseExpectation.value, DownloadExpectation.value). _setup also registers a Network.LoadingFailed handler and then awaits self.tab._register_handlers(), so Network is enabled on enter. The new _loading_failed_handler matches request_id, tears down all handlers, and sets ProtocolException(f'loading failed: {event.error_text}') on response_future and loading_finished_future if they are not done. It calls future.exception() so an unawaited future is not logged as never retrieved. _teardown removes the LoadingFailed handler. intercept.py: the 6 '(await self.response_future)' sites are wrapped in asyncio.shield.",
                "regression_test_path": "/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/BB-fixsafety/tests/test_r30.py",
                "fails_on_repo": "yes",
                "passes_on_prototype": "yes",
                "mypy_ok": "yes",
                "risks": "The exception type for a failed load (ProtocolException) is an API choice. Callers that used to catch only TimeoutError now get ProtocolException quickly. One exception instance is shared by two futures, so tracebacks accumulate if both are awaited (cosmetic). __aenter__ now makes a CDP round trip through _register_handlers. That function's bare 'except:' swallows CancelledError during __aenter__, an existing hazard shared with every send(). Re-entrancy: send(_is_update=True) -> aopen -> _register_handlers is nested but does not recurse, since network is appended before the send. No locks are involved. With shield, cancelling the caller no longer cancels the shared future, which is the intended change. Repo tests tests/core/test_tab.py + test_connection.py, including the external-marked expect/intercept tests: 47 passed. No new mypy errors."
              }
            }
