            "lens": "reproduce",
            "entry": {
              "group_id": "R42",
              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "All members reproduced on Python 3.13.16, with a fake CDP peer for the shared exception and remove_handlers, and real headless Chromium 141 for NaN and error data. (1) _fail_pending_transactions sets one ProtocolException instance on every pending tx. Each Connection.send appends its own command, so all three callers get the identical object, and its message lists all three commands and params, createTarget's token URL included. (2) NaN/Infinity params serialize to invalid JSON. Chrome answers with an id-less -32700 error, which the Listener logs as an unparseable event, and send() never returns (the tx stays in tab.mapper). (3) remove_handlers(cdp.network, h) and remove_handlers(cdp.network) remove nothing (44 event types still hold h). (4) ProtocolException drops error 'data', so str(e) lacks Chrome's 'Failed to deserialize params.url ...' explanation.",
              "member_verdicts": [
                {
                  "fid": "A1.4",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Fake peer drops getTargets/createTarget/getVersion, then aclose(). All three tasks got type=ProtocolException with the same id=140615076576320. Each str() was \"connection was closed\\ncommand:Target.getTargets\\nparams:{}\\ncommand:Target.createTarget\\nparams:{'url': 'https://secret.example/?token=abc'}\\ncommand:Browser.getVersion\\nparams:[]\", and 'res[0] is res[1] is res[2]: True'."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "A2.9",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Same root cause and same run as A1.4: one shared instance, with the message accumulating every pending command. _detach_session also passes a single ProtocolException('target session was detached') to _fail_pending_transactions (code reading)."
                },
                {
