              "group_id": "R28",
              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "util.filter_recurse (util.py:173) and filter_recurse_all (util.py:139) walk only .children and .shadow_roots[0], never .content_document. Elements inside same-origin iframes therefore cannot be found again after Element.update() (element.py:293). They lose .parent, keep a stale node_id (so element-scoped queries silently return []/None), remove_from_dom() does nothing without raising, and text search returns a parentless #text node plus a duplicate of its parent. All 6 members reproduced on real headless Chromium 141.",
