              "refinements": "The root cause is confirmed exactly as stated. Element.update() also replaces _tree with the top document even when the node is not found, so the element's real tree is lost. Separately, Element.update() does not refresh node_id when the lookup misses, and that is what turns the frame blind spot into silent []/None for scoped queries (via the __last one-shot retry in Tab.query_selector(_all)). A5.5(b) (container-scoped results get the container Element as node/tree) is a different root cause from the iframe one, and it is the same bug as R29/A8.8. Dedup across groups.",
