              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "I tried to refute this and could not. util.filter_recurse (util.py:173) and filter_recurse_all (util.py:139) only walk .children and shadow_roots[0]. With pierce=True, Chrome reports an IFRAME's document under .content_document and leaves the IFRAME's .children empty, so the helpers never reach a same-origin iframe's DOM. As a result Element.update() (element.py:293, filter_recurse at :323), Element.parent (:360), remove_from_dom (:279), the Tab.query_selector_all include_frames results (tab.py:615, created with tree=top doc) and the find_elements_by_text main loop (tab.py:715) all lose iframe nodes. All 6 members reproduced on headless Chromium 141 with Python 3.13.",
