              "summary": "Confirmed on real headless Chromium (Python 3.13). util.filter_recurse (util.py, filter_recurse ~L173) only walks .children and .shadow_roots[0]. DOM.getDocument(pierce=True) puts a same-origin iframe's document only under IFRAME.content_document, so every lookup by node_id or backend_node_id misses iframe nodes. Affected: Element.update, Element.parent, Element.remove_from_dom, Tab.query_selector(_all) result trees, and the main loop of Tab.find_elements_by_text. The minimal fix descends into content_document for raw cdp nodes inside filter_recurse only. Element.text opts out so it keeps textContent semantics. filter_recurse_all is left alone because Element.children already descends into iframes. On its own, the fix still leaves duplicate text matches; the R36 dedup removes them.",
