              "summary": "All 5 members reproduced on headless Chromium 141. (1) find_elements_by_text's iframe branch (tab.py:748-772) runs filter_recurse_all on an IFRAME Element. That yields Elements for normal children but raw cdp Nodes for anything under shadow_roots[0] (util.py:158-160), so `element.create(text_node.node, ...)` at tab.py:765 raises AttributeError. find/find_all/wait_for do not catch it. (2) Tab.query_selector (tab.py:622) has no content_document None guard: doc.node_id at :643 raises AttributeError for a cross-origin iframe, while query_selector_all has the guard added in #246. (3) In the except ProtocolException branches of query_selector(_all), the `_node is not None` path handles only 'could not find node' and has no else/raise, so element-scoped calls swallow other errors. (4) Element-scoped queries hand back an Element as .node and the container as .tree, so .parent is None.",
