              "refinements": "A6.2 only happens when the matching text sits inside a shadow root (open, or a user-agent one such as <input placeholder>) inside a same-origin iframe. The AttributeError escapes on the first attempt instead of retrying until the timeout, so one such match breaks every text search for that string on the page. Main-document shadow roots are not affected. A5.3 needs a user to call query_selector on an out-of-process iframe Element instead of using get_frame()/include_frames. That is a natural thing to try with captcha and payment frames. A5.8/B15.7 only matter for element-scoped calls, and they silently turn real errors (bad selector, detached session) into 'not found'; the tab-level API and select() raise correctly. A8.8 affects any container.query_selector(...).parent (direct children of the container and anything above them), and `await elem.update()` works around it.",
