          {
            "lens": "reproduce",
            "entry": {
              "group_id": "R37",
              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "Concurrent DOM queries on one tab silently return None/[]. Each call does its own DOM.getDocument (through Element.update() or Tab.query_selector(_all)), which invalidates the node ids of calls already in flight. The one-shot stale retry fails the same way and gives up quietly through the __last flag. A __last flag left on an Element after a successful retry makes its next stale failure return None with no retry. Reproduced on headless Chromium.",
              "member_verdicts": [
                {
                  "fid": "A5.2",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "With 20 rows from select_all('tr'), gather(row.query_selector('td')) returned None for 18 of 20 on 3 of 3 attempts, with 1 __last leftover each time. gather(row.query_selector_all('td')) was empty for 18 of 20. 10x gather tab.query_selector('#topp') gave 8 None. 10x gather tab.query_selector_all('p') gave lens [0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,2]. The same calls run sequentially gave 0 None. Leftover effect: after an extra getDocument, tab.query_selector('td', leftover_row) returned None with 0 update() calls (no retry), while a row without the flag recovered and returned the <TD>."
                }
              ],
              "evidence": "Python 3.13.16, Chromium 141.0.7390.37 headless. Command: cd <scratch> && PATH=<scratch>/bin:$PATH timeout 140 /home/user/zendriver/.venv/bin/python probe_r36_r37.py. Key lines: 'rows: 20', 'attempt 0: row.query_selector None count 18 of 20; __last leftovers 1' (and the same for attempts 1 and 2), 'row.query_selector_all empty count: 18 of 20', \"10x tab.query_selector('#topp') None count: 8\", \"10x tab.query_selector_all('p') lens: [0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 2, 2]\", 'sequential row.query_selector None count: 0', \"stale leftover-row tab.query_selector('td', row) -> None update() calls in retry: 0\", \"stale normal-row tab.query_selector('td', row) -> <TD ...>\". The stale-id mechanism is shown in probe_extra.py: 'direct DOM.querySelectorAll after update -> Could not find node with given id'. File: /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/BC-reproduce/probe_r36_r37.py.",
              "refinements": "Confirmed as stated, including the leftover __last side effect. Ran only on Python 3.13. The failure needs nothing beyond asyncio.gather on one tab, so I expect 3.10 to 3.12 to behave the same, but I did not run them. R36/A5.6 path (1) is another symptom of this same getDocument invalidation race.",
              "chrome_claims": [
                {
