                  "note": "Real Chromium, scaleX(-1): get_position() gives <Position(x=250, y=50, width=-100, height=40)>. Element.screenshot_b64 was still pending after 40s with a static page idle and also on a page with a running CSS animation. print_stack shows it parked at element.py:860 on <Transaction Page.captureScreenshot status: pending>. rotate(180deg) gives width=-100 and height=-40 and hangs. rotate(45deg) gives height=-42 and hangs too, so it is not only 180-degree or mirrored cases. rotate(90deg) gives width=0, and Chrome answers that at once with 'Cannot take screenshot with 0 width' (an error, not a hang). Raw captureScreenshot calls with width=-100 or height=-40 hang both with and without captureBeyondViewport. Connection.send has no timeout and Chrome keeps answering keepalive pings, so nothing upstream ends the wait. Refinement: the pending call is released only when the same tab later completes another valid screenshot. A DOM repaint or a running animation does not release it. In a normal sequential script it therefore hangs indefinitely."
