            "entry": {
              "group_id": "R32",
              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "All three element-screenshot bugs reproduce on real headless Chromium 141 with Python 3.13. (1) Position.__init__ unpacks fixed quad indices, so left=x4, right=x3, top=y2 and bottom=y4. For transform:scaleX(-1) this gives width=-100, and Element.screenshot_b64 then parks forever on the Page.captureScreenshot Transaction because Chrome never replies. For rotate(90deg) it gives width=0, which Chrome rejects with an error. (2) On a scrolled page the viewport-relative content quad is sent as a document-relative clip (capture_beyond_viewport=True), so the wrong region is captured. (3) Element.screenshot_b64/save_screenshot pass format='jpg' through unchanged and Chrome rejects it. A minimal local fix (bounding box of the quad, add cssVisualViewport.page_x/page_y, map jpg to jpeg) fixes all three.",
