              "refinements": "Only the mirrored case hangs. rotate(90deg) gives a zero width and an immediate Chrome error, not a hang. The scroll bug affects every element once the page is scrolled, including position:fixed and sticky ones. It does not show for below-the-fold elements on an unscrolled page, because viewport and document coordinates are then the same. Calling scroll_into_view() before a screenshot, which is a natural step, triggers it. With fixed indices, Position.center is also wrong for rotated elements (by 20px for the rotate(90deg) quad), which affects mouse_click/mouse_move/flash. The bounding-box fix corrects that too. For scaleX(-1) the centre is the same either way. flash() still positions its dot from viewport coordinates with position:absolute, so it is misplaced on scrolled pages (cosmetic, not fixed here). The hang itself is Chrome not answering a negative-size clip, and Connection.send has no timeout. A raw tab.send(capture_screenshot(clip with negative width)) would still hang.",
