              "group_id": "R33",
              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "Element.apply always sends returnByValue=true and only checks result[0], which is always a truthy RemoteObject. So a throwing function returns None, a rejected promise returns {}, and the exceptionDetails branch is dead. return_by_value=False returns a RemoteObject without object_id. Because errors are swallowed, the b506c8f change to HTMLInputElement.prototype's value setter makes clear_input and clear_input_by_deleting silent no-ops on <textarea> ('Illegal invocation'). All of this reproduces on real Chromium. A small local fix (unpack the tuple, raise ProtocolException on exceptionDetails like Tab.evaluate does, pass return_by_value through, look the value setter up on the element's own prototype chain) fixes it. Raising is a visible behaviour change, and it would surface a further pre-existing silent failure (clear_input_by_deleting on <input type=email>), which the prototype guards against.",
