              "fix_assessment": {
                "kind": "minimal-local",
                "prototype_dir": "/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/BD-fixsafety/pkg",
                "diff_summary": "zendriver/core/element.py. Element.apply: pass return_by_value=return_by_value to call_function_on; 'remote_object, errors = result'; 'if errors: raise ProtocolException(errors)' (local import from .connection, as screenshot_b64 and flash already do); return remote_object.value or remote_object. clear_input: walk Object.getPrototypeOf(el) up to the first own 'value' descriptor and call its setter, falling back to el.value=''. clear_input_by_deleting: the same prototype-chain lookup for nativeSetter, with setSelectionRange in try/catch.",
                "regression_test_path": "/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/BD-fixsafety/tests/test_r33.py",
                "fails_on_repo": "yes",
                "passes_on_prototype": "yes",
                "mypy_ok": "yes",
                "risks": "No locks or re-entrancy are involved. The visible behaviour change is that apply() now raises ProtocolException on a JS exception or rejected promise, as Tab.evaluate already does. Everything built on apply (focus, send_keys's focus, select_option, __call__, is_recording, record_video, get_js_attributes, clear_input*) can now raise where it used to return silently. Whether to raise or to return the ExceptionDetails is the API decision the triage mentions. Raising matches Tab.evaluate, and the old 'return result[1]' branch was dead anyway. return_by_value=False now returns a live handle with object_id and value=None for objects, where it used to return value={}. No in-repo caller passes False. The prototype-chain lookup still skips React's instance-level tracker property, so the React tests pass. The setter's realm is the element's own, so it also works for elements in iframes. No new mypy errors."
              }
            }
          }
        ]
