              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "All members reproduce browser-free with a fake tab and a real cdp.dom.Node on Python 3.13. _make_attrs stores 'class' as 'class_', so get('class') and el['class'] return None. Element.__setattr__ checks key[1:] ('ree') instead of '_tree', so el.tree = doc lands in attrs and _tree stays None. copy.copy, copy.deepcopy and pickle recurse through __getattr__, get, attrs and the missing _attrs until RecursionError. highlight_overlay's getattr(self, '_is_highlighted', False) goes through the @deprecated __getattr__, so it fails under -W error::DeprecationWarning before sending any command.",
