                  "fid": "B16.10",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Real Chromium: after `async with await zd.start(headless=True) as b:`, b.stopped is False and the Chrome pid is still alive. Three loop iterations left three Chrome processes alive inside the event loop. Refute angle: asyncio_atexit's _atexit_cleanup killed all of them when asyncio.run() returned. The two examples that use the pattern (examples/wait_for_page.py and expect_download.py) are single-run scripts and are only lightly affected. The leak is real for loops that open one browser per job. At loop close the cleanup also logged 'Executor shutdown has been called' for each browser (the atexit profile issue owned elsewhere). Additional: __aexit__'s `raise exc_type(exc_val)` replaced a user exception whose constructor takes 2 arguments with a TypeError."
                }
