              "evidence": "Probes are in /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/BD-refute/r46/: probe_r46.py (save_to_dom, hashing, evaluate, handle growth), probe_leak2.py and probe_leak3.py (detached-node retention, renderer USS via psutil), probe_intercept.py (www/ test server, nested intercept), probe_aexit.py. Key output: 'outerHTML: <div id=\"cmt\" data-x=\"1\">&lt;#comment &gt;<!--#comment--><i>it</i></div>'; '[set(select_all('a'))] EXC TypeError: unhashable type: 'Element''; '[evaluate(1/0)] OK -> None'; 'after 400 apply on fresh 200KB nodes: 136 MB' against 'after control 400 (no apply): 43 MB'; 'a got url: .../b.json'; '[title] TIMEOUT 8s' inside the outer block; 'after async with #0: stopped=False ... alive=True'; 'after asyncio.run (atexit cleanup ran): [(24319, False), ...]'.",
              "refinements": "These are design-level items with mixed severities. The worst runtime effect is A10.2 scenario 2: inside an outer intercept, every request pauses and the page load stalls until the block exits. A8.13 is bounded by navigation or context destruction and costs almost nothing for repeated handles to the same live node; it matters only when apply, click or update run on nodes that are later removed in a long-lived page. B16.10 is bounded by asyncio_atexit at event-loop close, so single-run scripts are unaffected and per-job loops in one event loop pile up Chrome processes. A8.17 and A7.11 fail loudly with TypeError and never silently. A6.9 has a workaround (return_by_value=False). Browser.__aexit__ and Connection.__aexit__ also rebuild exceptions with exc_type(exc_val), which breaks exceptions whose constructor takes several arguments.",
