              ],
              "evidence": "Probes /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/BD-fixsafety/probe_r46.py and probe_a10.py on the repo copy printed the outputs quoted per member, e.g. '[A8.13] 500 applies -> 500 distinct object ids; first id still resolves: value=inp', '[B16.10] after async with: stopped=False pid 30521 alive=True', 'S2 tab.get TIMEOUT (8s)', 'S2 outer a resolved with: http://127.0.0.1:42315/page2.html ResourceType.DOCUMENT'. Regression test tests/test_r46.py (7 tests: element hash, tab hash, evaluate unserializable, save_to_dom x3, async-with stop). On the repo: '7 failed in 4.15s'. On the prototype (zendriver from .../BD-fixsafety/pkg46/zendriver/__init__.py): '7 passed in 4.21s'. The repo's own test_tab, test_browser, test_frames, test_multiple_browsers and test_react_controlled_input pass on pkg46 (75 passed). There are no tests for A8.13 or A10.2, which were not prototyped.",
              "refinements": "A8.10: when DOM.setOuterHTML rejects the markup it still applies part of it (title truncated to 'say '), so save_to_dom corrupts the DOM and also raises. setOuterHTML does keep node identity (backend id and isConnected unchanged), so that part is not a bug. A10.2: checking the pattern in _response_handler is not enough on its own. The inner Fetch.enable replaces the tab's pattern list, so the outer request is never paused at all. The second scenario hangs any later tab.get/page load because every request pauses with no one continuing it. A6.9: Element.apply has the same gap. B16.10: Browser.__aexit__ also re-raises via exc_type(exc_val), which rebuilds the exception and loses its traceback. That is separate, and I did not change it. Browser.stop() is idempotent, so an explicit stop() after the block stays safe.",
              "chrome_claims": [
                {
                  "claim": "CDP returns unserializableValue for Infinity/NaN/-0/BigInt with returnByValue",
