              "fix_assessment": {
                "kind": "design-api",
                "prototype_dir": "/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/BD-fixsafety/pkg46",
                "diff_summary": "Prototyped (pkg46, independent of pkg). element.py save_to_dom: diff self.attrs (mapping class_ to class) against node.attributes and send DOM.setAttributeValue or DOM.removeAttribute per attribute instead of DOM.setOuterHTML(str(self)). element.py: __hash__ returning hash(self.backend_node_id). tab.py: Tab.__hash__ returning hash(self.target_id), with __eq__ unchanged (equal targets imply equal ids). tab.py evaluate: when value is None and unserializable_value is set, return util.parse_unserializable_value(...), a new util.py helper doing int(v[:-1]) for 'n'-suffixed values and float(v) otherwise. browser.py __aexit__: await self.stop() before the existing re-raise. Not prototyped (design): A8.13 needs a handle lifecycle, such as resolve_node with an object_group per element plus Runtime.releaseObjectGroup, or releasing the previous handle when self._remote_object is replaced. A10.2 needs a per-tab interception registry: Fetch.enable with the union of active patterns, re-enable with the remaining patterns on teardown and Fetch.disable only when none remain, handlers that match their own url_pattern/resource_type/stage, and _register_handlers never auto-enabling cdp.fetch without patterns while interceptions exist.",
                "regression_test_path": "/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/BD-fixsafety/tests/test_r46.py",
                "fails_on_repo": "yes",
                "passes_on_prototype": "yes",
                "mypy_ok": "yes",
                "risks": "Hash: Element hash is stable (backend_node_id survives update()) and consistent with __eq__. Elements of different tabs with the same backend id are already equal, so they also hash equal. The Tab hash is stable because target_id never changes for a Tab, and class-body definitions are allowed under the CantTouchThis metaclass. evaluate: callers that got None for Infinity/NaN/-0/BigInt now get float/int, and NaN != NaN may surprise equality checks. __aexit__: `async with browser:` now ends the browser, and code that kept using the browser after the block would break. The only in-repo use (examples/wait_for_page.py) is scoped correctly, and stop() is idempotent. save_to_dom: it now writes only attributes, never children (Element has no API to change children anyway), and it no longer reverts attribute changes the page made to attributes the user did not touch. The stale-node_id risk is the same as before. A8.13 risk: releasing handles races with concurrent apply() on the same element and invalidates el.object_id or handles the user holds, so it needs an API decision. A10.2 needs a registry and a decision about who continues unmatched paused requests, otherwise they hang. No new mypy errors on pkg46."
              }
            }
          }
