        "lenses": [
          {
            "lens": "reproduce",
            "entry": {
              "group_id": "R38",
              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "All four keys.py defects reproduce in real headless Chromium 141 (Python 3.13). (1) Grapheme clusters of 4 or more UTF-16 units are sent as a single char event, Chrome rejects them, and typing stops partway through. (2) Modifiers are released before the main key and in press order, so the main keyup carries no modifiers. (3) to_cdp_events mutates self.key, so a reused KeyEvents types a different character the second time. (4) SpecialKeys.SPACE sends code ' ', so the page sees e.code === ''.",
              "member_verdicts": [
                {
                  "fid": "A10.5",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Real Chromium, textarea.send_keys('x'+s+'y'). '👍' (2 units) works and the value becomes 'x👍y'. '👍🏽' (4 units), '🇩🇪' (4) and the family ZWJ emoji (11) each raise ProtocolException \"Invalid 'text' parameter [code: -32602]\" on Input.dispatchKeyEvent{type:'char', text:<whole grapheme>}, and the value is left as 'x'. from_mixed_input(['Hi 👍🏽!']) fails the same way and leaves 'Hi '. The cause is in KeyEvents.from_text / to_cdp_events (the CHAR branch for emoji): the grapheme library returns the whole cluster as one grapheme, and that cluster goes out as one char event."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "A10.9",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Document keydown/keypress/keyup logger. from_mixed_input(['A']) logs keydown Shift, keydown 'A' shift=true, keypress 'A', keyup Shift, keyup 'a' shift=false. Ctrl+Enter logs keydown Control, keydown Enter ctrl=true, keypress, keyup Control, keyup Enter ctrl=false. Ctrl+Shift+a releases Control before Shift (press order, not reverse), and the final keyup 'a' has shift=false, ctrl=false. In KeyEvents.to_down_up_sequence, step 3 clears all modifiers before step 4 sends the main keyup."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "A10.10",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Offline: ev=KeyEvents('A'). The first to_cdp_events(DOWN_AND_UP) gives [Shift down, 'A' down text 'A' mods 8, Shift up, 'a' up], and afterwards ev.key=='a'. The second call gives ['a' down text 'a' mods 0, 'a' up]. KeyEvents('!') reused gives '1'. In real Chromium the second use logs only 'a' events with shift=false, and the textarea holds 'a'. The CHAR path also mutates the key: after one to_cdp_events(CHAR) on KeyEvents(SpecialKeys.ENTER), self.key is the str '\\n'. Mutation sites: to_cdp_events (`self.key, override_modifiers = self._normalise_key(...)`) and _get_key_and_text (`self.key = self.conv_to_str(...)`)."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "A10.11",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Real Chromium logger. send_keys(SpecialKeys.SPACE) and from_mixed_input([' ']) both log keydown \" \" with an empty code and keyCode 32. The control send_keys(SpecialKeys.TAB) logs code 'Tab'. The generated payload has code=' ' because SpecialKeys.SPACE = (' ', 32) is used as the (code, keyCode) pair, both in _handle_special_key_lookup and in _handle_string_key_lookup for ' '."
                }
              ],
              "evidence": "Commands: `cd /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/BE-reproduce && PATH=<scratchpad>/bin:$PATH timeout 120 /home/user/zendriver/.venv/bin/python probe_keys.py` (real headless Chromium 141.0.7390.37, page site/keys.html served by a local http.server) and `/home/user/zendriver/.venv/bin/python probe_keys_offline.py`. Key output: `A10.5 '👍🏽' utf16=4 -> EXC ProtocolException Invalid 'text' parameter ... [code: -32602]; value='x'`; `A10.9 Ctrl+Enter: [keydown Control ctrl=true, keydown Enter ctrl=true, keypress Enter, keyup Control ctrl=false, keyup Enter ctrl=false]`; `A10.10 second use: [keydown \"a\" shift=false ...]; textarea after second: a`; `A10.11 SpecialKeys.SPACE: keydown:\" \"::32` (empty code) vs `TAB: keydown:\"Tab\":Tab:9`. Offline: `p2: [('keyDown','a','a',0),('keyUp','a','a',0)]`, `SPACE events: [('keyDown',' ',' ',32),...]`.",
              "refinements": "A10.5: the call stops at the first long grapheme, so earlier characters are typed and later ones are lost; the field is left partly filled. Emoji of 2 units or fewer work. A10.9: besides the missing modifiers on the main keyup, each modifier keyup reports modifier state with its own flag cleared (Shift up reports shift=false) while the others are still set. A10.10: the CHAR-path mutation also turns a SpecialKeys member into a str, which changes later DOWN_AND_UP events (ENTER mutated to '\\n' still maps back to Enter).",
              "chrome_claims": [
                {
                  "claim": "Chrome rejects Input.dispatchKeyEvent char text of 4 or more UTF-16 units with Invalid 'text' parameter",
                  "status": "verified",
                  "how": "Real headless Chromium 141 returned -32602 for '👍🏽', '🇩🇪' and the family emoji, and accepted '👍'."
                },
