              "refinements": "A10.5 is wider than emoji: any grapheme of 4 or more UTF-16 units fails, combining-mark sequences included, because every grapheme without a keyCode is forced onto the CHAR path. The exact limit is text16.size() >= 4 (3 accepted, 4 rejected). A10.10: the CHAR-path mutation mostly changes only the key's type, since SpecialKeys becomes str, but it is still a mutation. Seen in passing and not part of this group: Ctrl+Shift+a reports keydown key 'a' with shiftKey=true, because _handle_printable_char only upper-cases when modifiers == Shift exactly.",
