            "lens": "fixsafety",
            "entry": {
              "group_id": "R39",
              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "All 7 distinct Tab bugs reproduce on real headless Chromium 141, except A7.8, which is Windows-only and was reproduced by emulating Windows text mode plus a Chromium render check. (1) get_all_urls joins against scheme://host and drops bare relative links and any value containing '#'. (2) set_user_agent without metadata empties navigator.userAgentData, headless and headful. (3) download_file %-formats url and filename into JS: a quote silently does nothing, and a crafted filename runs JS. (4) save_snapshot text mode turns CRLF into CRCRLF on Windows, which renders blank. (5) save_screenshot(format='webp') raises UnboundLocalError. (6) Two auto-named screenshots in the same second share one path. (7) print_to_pdf(transfer_mode='ReturnAsStream') writes 0 bytes.",
              "member_verdicts": [
                {
                  "fid": "A7.5",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Page /docs/index.html. get_all_urls() returns /sub/page.html, /images/a.png, /up.html, /root.html. The browser resolves the links to /docs/style.css, /docs/sub/page.html, /docs/images/a.png, /docs/other.html, /up.html, /root.html and https://example.org/page#frag. So style.css and other.html are dropped, the #frag URL is dropped, and two URLs resolve to the wrong place."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "A12.7",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
