              "refinements": "get_all_urls should resolve against document.baseURI so that <base href> is honoured, which the prototype does. Anchors made only of '#' are still skipped as in-page links. The old filter also accepted javascript:, mailto: and data: values only when they contained '/', and the urljoin+startswith filter still drops those. A7.6 needs a design decision for headful mode: there is no stored metadata to reuse. Reading navigator.userAgentData.getHighEntropyValues only works in secure contexts. Sending user_agent='' keeps the hints but drops a custom UA the caller set earlier, and in headless it restores HeadlessChrome. So the prototype only fixes the case where the current UA equals browser.headless_user_agent[0], which is the regression the CHANGELOG fix was meant to remove. A7.7's injection actually executes. A7.7 also notes that fetch errors are swallowed because the inner promise is neither awaited nor returned; the prototype leaves that alone, since awaiting it would change download_file's timing and error behaviour.",
