            "entry": {
              "group_id": "R31",
              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "Chrome applies the download behaviour to a whole browser context. Without browserContextId it uses the default context, even when the command is sent on a context tab's session, and a call without eventsEnabled turns off DownloadWillBegin for that session. zendriver sends every call without browser_context_id and keeps the state per Tab (Connection._download_behavior). Confirmed on real Chromium: (1) download_file inside expect_download turns the events off, so ex.value hangs, and the file is downloaded despite the deny. (2) set_download_path and expect_download do nothing for create_context tabs, and the expectation hangs. (3) One tab's download_file or expect_download exit overwrites the path another tab set. The right fix is a design change: per-context state, the context id sent for non-default contexts, events kept on, and a per-context count of active expectations.",
              "member_verdicts": [
