                "prototype_dir": "/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/BE-fixsafety/R31/pkg",
                "diff_summary": "browser.py: Browser._download_behaviors: dict[context_id|None, list|None] and Browser._download_expectations: dict[context_id|None, int]. connection.py: the class attribute _download_behavior becomes a property/setter backed by the owner's dict keyed by self.browser_context_id, with an instance fallback when there is no owner. New _count_download_expectations(delta) and async _set_download_behavior(behavior, path): it calls Target.getBrowserContexts on the browser connection, passes browser_context_id only for non-default contexts, and always sends events_enabled=True. tab.py: set_download_path uses _set_download_behavior. download_file sets the default ./downloads path only when no state is recorded and no expectation is active in the context, so the deny holds. expect.py DownloadExpectation: __aenter__ increments the count (decrementing again if the send fails) and denies through _set_download_behavior. __aexit__ decrements, and at 0 restores the context's current recorded state ('default' if none), removing the handler in a finally. element.py record_video uses _set_download_behavior and records the state.",
                "regression_test_path": "/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/BE-fixsafety/R31/tests/test_r31_download.py",
                "fails_on_repo": "yes",
                "passes_on_prototype": "yes",
                "mypy_ok": "yes",
                "risks": "No asyncio locks, so no deadlock or re-entrancy issue. Cancel paths: __aenter__ decrements on BaseException, and __aexit__ always removes the handler. Changes callers would notice: state is shared across tabs of a context, so one tab's set_download_path affects download_file on its siblings, which matches Chrome. Download events stay enabled, so DownloadProgress events reach sessions with no handler, a small amount of traffic. Each download-behaviour call costs one extra Target.getBrowserContexts round trip. Inside an expect_download block, download_file without a path is now denied instead of written to ./downloads. An explicit set_download_path inside the block still re-allows downloads immediately. _download_behavior becomes a property on Connection, which is private API. The naive per-context version (capture at enter, restore at exit) leaves the context denied after overlapping expectations, as shown above, so the counter is required. mypy: 332 errors, the same as an untouched copy. ruff is clean."
              }
            }
