            "lens": "reproduce",
            "entry": {
              "group_id": "R43",
              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "All four cloudflare/proxy members reproduced with my own probes. (1) verify_cf raises 'Error checking input element' after a click that solves the challenge and navigates away. This ran on real headless Chromium 141. (2) With an https:// upstream, the forwarder keeps the tunnel and the _handle_client task alive after the client closes. An http:// upstream tears down at once. (3) UnicodeError from IDNA encoding and ValueError from urlsplit/url.port escape _handle_client. The client gets an empty response, not a 502, and asyncio logs 'Unhandled exception in client_connected_cb'. (4) A handshake timeout is reported as 'proxy closed the connection: TimeoutError()' on Python 3.11 and later.",
              "member_verdicts": [
                {
                  "fid": "A11.2",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Real Chromium. The page has a closed shadow root whose div has data-src=challenges.cloudflare.com and a click listener that sets location.href='/solved', plus a light-DOM input[name=cf-turnstile-response]. In navigate mode verify_cf(click_delay=1, timeout=10) raised \"Exception: Error checking input element: Node with given id does not belong to the document command:DOM.resolveNode params:{'backendNodeId': BackendNodeId(10)} [code: -32000].\" and the final url was /solved. Controls: remove mode returned OK after 1.02s and value mode returned OK after 1.02s. The raise comes from `await input_el` (Element.update -> DOM.resolveNode with the stale backend id) inside verify_cf.check_input, which runs before the 'not fresh_input' success branch."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "A11.3",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Fake CONNECT proxy that acts as the origin and closes only after it sees EOF, run with and without TLS on the same handler. Output: tls=False: 0 forwarder client tasks alive 2s after the client closed, origin_saw_eof=True. tls=True: 1 alive after 2s and still 1 after 10s, origin_saw_eof=False. The stuck task is at ProxyForwarder._handle_client -> _forward, waiting on the pipe() gather. Root cause confirmed: copy_stream skips write_eof because the asyncio SSL transport's can_write_eof() is False, so the upstream never learns of the close. How long it lasts in practice depends on when the upstream or origin sends data or closes; not measured against real servers."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "A11.7",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "socks5 upstream, minimal fake SOCKS5 server. Four inputs gave response=b'' and 'LOG ERROR asyncio: Unhandled exception in client_connected_cb': CONNECT with a 64-char label (UnicodeEncodeError: label too long), CONNECT a..b.com:443 (UnicodeEncodeError: label empty), GET http://example.com:99999/ (ValueError: Port out of range 0-65535), and GET http://[bad/ (ValueError: Invalid IPv6 URL). The last one raises in urlsplit before any upstream is chosen, so it happens with any upstream type. Control: CONNECT nohostport gives 'HTTP/1.1 400 Proxy Error' plus a warning."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "A11.9",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "With proxy.TIMEOUT=0.5 and an upstream that accepts TCP but never replies, open_tunnel raised ProxyError('proxy closed the connection: TimeoutError()') for both http and socks5 upstreams, with cause TimeoutError. issubclass(asyncio.TimeoutError, OSError) is True on Python 3.13.16 and 3.11.17. Python 3.10 was not available; there asyncio.TimeoutError is not an OSError, so the message should be correct (reasoned only). The status stays 502, so this is cosmetic."
                }
              ],
              "evidence": "Python 3.13.16, Chromium 141.0.7390.37. Every probe printed __file__ = /home/user/zendriver/zendriver/...\n1) cd /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/BF-reproduce/r43 && PATH=<scratchpad>/bin:$PATH; for m in navigate remove value; do timeout 120 /home/user/zendriver/.venv/bin/python cf_nav.py $m; done\n -> MODE=navigate: verify_cf RAISED Exception: Error checking input element: Node with given id does not belong to the document ... DOM.resolveNode ... final url: http://127.0.0.1:38265/solved\n -> MODE=remove: verify_cf returned OK after 1.02s ; MODE=value: returned OK after 1.02s\n2) timeout 120 .venv/bin/python proxy_leak.py (self-signed cert from openssl)\n -> tls=False: forwarder client tasks alive 2s after client closed: 0; origin_saw_eof=True\n -> tls=True: ... alive 2s ...: 1; origin_saw_eof=False (stack: proxy.py:228 _handle_client await self._forward, wait_for=_GatheringFuture pending)\n -> tls=True: ... alive 10s ...: 1; origin_saw_eof=False\n3) timeout 120 .venv/bin/python proxy_errs.py\n -> long-label CONNECT: response=b'' / LOG ERROR asyncio: Unhandled exception in client_connected_cb / UnicodeEncodeError ... label too long\n -> empty-label CONNECT, GET bad port (socks), GET bad ipv6 url: same pattern (UnicodeEncodeError label empty / ValueError Port out of range / ValueError Invalid IPv6 URL)\n -> control: bad CONNECT target: response=b'HTTP/1.1 400 Proxy Error...'\n -> handshake timeout (http|socks5) -> ProxyError('proxy closed the connection: TimeoutError()') cause=TimeoutError; TimeoutError is OSError subclass: True\n4) /usr/bin/python3.11 -c 'issubclass(asyncio.TimeoutError, OSError)' -> 3.11.17 True",
              "refinements": "A11.2: the failing call is the `await input_el` (Element.update) inside the try in verify_cf.check_input, which runs before the fresh query. Any DOM.resolveNode failure after checkbox_clicked=True (a new document) should count as success, or the fresh query should run first. A11.3: Chrome closes the socket fully. The forwarder keeps the client side half-open because StreamReaderProtocol keeps the transport open on EOF. The tunnel is released only when the upstream sends something (the write to the dead client then fails) or closes. My fake never does, so it was still alive at 10s. Real duration depends on the origin and proxy idle timeouts and on whether the inner TLS sends close_notify; not verified. A11.7: also covers the empty label, and ValueError from urlsplit (any upstream) and url.port (socks branch, _forward). The log line text is from Python 3.12+ streams; older versions log 'Task exception was never retrieved' instead (not run). A11.9: the TimeoutError branch in open_tunnel is dead code on 3.11+.",
