            "lens": "fixsafety",
            "entry": {
              "group_id": "R45",
              "verdict": "confirmed",
              "summary": "All members reproduce. circle() treats y=0 as missing (`if not y`). html_from_tree appends each child's outer HTML (which already contains its descendants) and then recurses, so a node at depth d appears d times; confirmed in real Chromium. add_extension(dir) keeps overwriting path in the rglob('manifest.*') loop and ends on the last nested match. add_extension(.crx) extracts into a mkdtemp directory that nothing ever removes; confirmed with a real browser start/stop and after the process exits. A9.11 and B16.17 are the same defect.",
              "member_verdicts": [
                {
                  "fid": "A9.8",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "circle(100, 0, radius=10, num=4) gives y values around 80, identical to circle(100, 100). The other part of the claim, that the circle is centred at (x-2r, y-2r), is confirmed as behaviour, but the docstring calls x and y the 'start' position. That is ambiguous, so I did not treat it as a bug or change it."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "A9.9",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Real Chromium, data:text/html,<p>hello</p>: html_from_tree gives '<html><head></head><body><p>hello</p></body></html><head></head><body><p>hello</p></body><p>hello</p>hello', while get_content gives '<html>...</html>'. Not used inside zendriver; it is a public util."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "A9.7",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Root manifest.json plus web/manifest.webmanifest: _extensions == [<root>/web]. A nested assets/page/manifest.json is picked the same way."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "A9.11",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Real headless browser: config.add_extension(ext.crx), zd.start, stop. The extracted /tmp/extension_* still exists after browser.stop() and after the Python process exits. grep: the only rmtree in core is the temp profile cleanup in browser.py."
                },
                {
                  "fid": "B16.17",
                  "verdict": "confirmed",
                  "note": "Duplicate of A9.11; same evidence."
                }
              ],
              "evidence": "Regression test /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/BF-fixsafety/tests/test_r45_util_config.py, browser-free (FakeTab answers DOM.getOuterHTML; Config(browser_executable_path='/bin/true')). Repo code (zendriver from /home/user/zendriver/zendriver/__init__.py): '5 failed, 1 passed'. Prototype (zendriver from .../BF-fixsafety/R45/pkg/zendriver/__init__.py): '6 passed'. Real-Chromium probes (.../probe/html_real.py, .../probe/crx_real.py): the repo duplicates the HTML and the prototype matches get_content; the crx dir exists after the process exits on the repo ('yes') but not on the prototype ('no'). The repo's tests/core/test_config.py on the prototype: 9 passed.",
              "refinements": "Config is documented as reusable as a template for several browsers ('config can be used/reused as a template for multiple browser instances'). So deleting the extracted crx in Browser.stop would break other or later browsers that share the Config. The safe owner is the Config itself: weakref.finalize, which runs on GC or at interpreter exit.",
              "chrome_claims": [
                {
                  "claim": "html_from_tree output repeats subtrees compared with tab.get_content()",
                  "status": "verified",
                  "how": "Real headless Chromium probe on the repo and the prototype"
                },
                {
                  "claim": "The extracted crx dir survives browser.stop() and process exit",
                  "status": "verified",
                  "how": "Real headless Chromium start/stop with a zipped manifest.json .crx; checked the dir after the subprocess exited"
                }
              ],
              "realism": "medium",
              "severity": "wrong-result",
              "fix_assessment": {
                "kind": "minimal-local",
                "prototype_dir": "/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/BF-fixsafety/R45/pkg",
                "diff_summary": "util.py: circle uses `if y is None: y = x`; html_from_tree drops the recursive call after appending each child's outer HTML. config.py: import shutil and weakref; add_extension(.crx) registers weakref.finalize(self, shutil.rmtree, tf, ignore_errors=True) right after mkdtemp; add_extension(dir) keeps path when path/'manifest.json' is a file, otherwise uses the shallowest rglob('manifest.json') match (sorted by len(parts), first one).",
                "regression_test_path": "/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-zendriver/b2021b39-94e6-5220-9e66-7f33c0314a80/scratchpad/verify/BF-fixsafety/tests/test_r45_util_config.py",
                "fails_on_repo": "yes",
                "passes_on_prototype": "yes",
                "mypy_ok": "yes",
                "risks": "circle(x, 0) now really uses y=0, a change for callers who relied on the old fallback (unlikely). html_from_tree output shrinks to the de-duplicated HTML. add_extension now looks only for manifest.json (Chrome requires exactly that name), not manifest.*. The crx dir is removed when the Config is garbage-collected or at interpreter exit: if a user builds args from a Config, drops the Config and launches Chrome by hand, the dir can vanish; if a script exits while Chrome is still running, the files are deleted under it. The finalizer is registered before extraction, so a bad zip no longer leaks the dir either. No async or locking involved."
              }
            }
          }
        ]
